1
00:00:00,898 --> 00:00:03,668
(I'm Doing Great on My Own)

2
00:00:04,268 --> 00:00:06,467
(A radio show is in full swing in the booth.)

3
00:00:06,468 --> 00:00:07,738
Peanut butter cream bun.

4
00:00:07,868 --> 00:00:09,838
- It's "Hope Song at Noon." - Yes, it is.

5
00:00:10,368 --> 00:00:11,437
"Hope Song at Noon."

6
00:00:11,438 --> 00:00:12,507
She's been hosting it...

7
00:00:12,508 --> 00:00:13,638
- for 15 years. - Right.

8
00:00:14,108 --> 00:00:15,678
- At noon. - For 15 years?

9
00:00:15,748 --> 00:00:17,607
I spent my 30s, hosting this show.

10
00:00:17,608 --> 00:00:18,648
Yes.

11
00:00:19,018 --> 00:00:21,147
This is your DJ, Kim Shin Young, from "Hope Song at Noon."

12
00:00:21,148 --> 00:00:22,317
And DJ Choi Yoo Jung.

13
00:00:22,318 --> 00:00:23,318
- Thank you. - Thank you.

14
00:00:23,818 --> 00:00:25,047
- Good work today. - You should go.

15
00:00:25,048 --> 00:00:26,558
- See you next week. - Sure.

16
00:00:27,158 --> 00:00:29,927
I'll make you a great dessert next time.

17
00:00:29,928 --> 00:00:30,958
Sounds good.

18
00:00:31,258 --> 00:00:33,097
- Good work. - Good work.

19
00:00:33,098 --> 00:00:34,698
- Great job. - Good work.

20
00:00:35,128 --> 00:00:37,228
- Great job today. - See you tomorrow morning.

21
00:00:37,298 --> 00:00:38,927
- See you tomorrow. - Bye.

22
00:00:38,928 --> 00:00:40,898
Bye, I'm off.

23
00:00:41,368 --> 00:00:43,107
Do you win the Golden Mouth Award when you host a show for 10 years?

24
00:00:43,108 --> 00:00:44,108
- Twenty years. - Twenty years?

25
00:00:44,109 --> 00:00:46,137
I already won the Bronze Mouth Award after my tenth year.

26
00:00:46,138 --> 00:00:48,838
I was the youngest winner of the Bronze Mouth Award then.

27
00:00:49,278 --> 00:00:51,918
It was the first show hosted by a solo female DJ to win the award.

28
00:00:52,208 --> 00:00:54,008
- It was the first show ever. - That's crazy.

29
00:00:54,048 --> 00:00:55,718
If nothing...

30
00:00:56,548 --> 00:00:58,594
- If you keep working... Yes. - crazy happens until 2029,

31
00:00:58,618 --> 00:00:59,787
- then... - It's as long as you don't quit.

32
00:00:59,788 --> 00:01:02,457
Right. As long as I don't quit, I'll win the Golden Mouth Award.

33
00:01:02,458 --> 00:01:04,187
- That's impressive. - That's crazy.

34
00:01:04,188 --> 00:01:06,928
Hosting a radio show for two years and a half was really tough.

35
00:01:06,998 --> 00:01:08,327
- I could never go on my vacation. - Right.

36
00:01:08,328 --> 00:01:09,367
- Vacation. - That's really tough.

37
00:01:09,368 --> 00:01:10,427
- I mean, you could. - As for me,

38
00:01:10,428 --> 00:01:12,227
hosting it for a special DJ for a week was tough.

39
00:01:12,228 --> 00:01:13,367
That was tough for you?

40
00:01:13,368 --> 00:01:15,198
- Why bother living then? - Seriously.

41
00:01:15,298 --> 00:01:17,338
The radio show becomes part of my life.

42
00:01:18,038 --> 00:01:19,408
- Like a permanent job. - Right.

43
00:01:20,878 --> 00:01:25,678
(The worker with a permanent job quickly gets off work.)

44
00:01:26,818 --> 00:01:28,648
You're getting off work right on time again.

45
00:01:29,318 --> 00:01:31,047
(Coughing)

46
00:01:31,048 --> 00:01:33,818
- Wait, you must be sick. - I've been sick lately.

47
00:01:33,988 --> 00:01:35,217
It started with a pollen allergy...

48
00:01:35,218 --> 00:01:36,488
- and rhinitis. - Right.

49
00:01:36,658 --> 00:01:38,528
It turned out I had a throat infection.

50
00:01:39,158 --> 00:01:41,297
- Throat infections are so painful. - It really was.

51
00:01:41,298 --> 00:01:42,727
- Especially for DJs who must talk. - Yes.

52
00:01:42,728 --> 00:01:44,597
- That's the worst. - My condition was the worst then.

53
00:01:44,598 --> 00:01:46,437
- It's really painful. - It was the worst that day.

54
00:01:46,438 --> 00:01:47,597
- Ji Hyeon, you also had it... - But you still went to work.

55
00:01:47,598 --> 00:01:48,937
- when you had your concert. - Yes.

56
00:01:48,938 --> 00:01:50,767
- You could barely talk then. - I thought it'd be the end of me.

57
00:01:50,768 --> 00:01:52,437
- It really hurt. - Right.

58
00:01:52,438 --> 00:01:53,677
- Throat infections last quite long. - Right.

59
00:01:53,678 --> 00:01:55,408
- They last at least a month. - Yes.

60
00:01:57,848 --> 00:01:59,878
Hello. Have a good day.

61
00:02:01,578 --> 00:02:02,847
(Coughing)

62
00:02:02,848 --> 00:02:05,348
My goodness.

63
00:02:06,488 --> 00:02:07,558
Okay.

64
00:02:08,488 --> 00:02:09,588
All right.

65
00:02:10,028 --> 00:02:15,297
(Because of the throat infection, driving herself home is tough too.)

66
00:02:15,298 --> 00:02:17,798
That's all

67
00:02:18,298 --> 00:02:20,268
- Do you drive yourself around? - Yes.

68
00:02:20,468 --> 00:02:21,938
I see.

69
00:02:22,168 --> 00:02:23,168
Clap!

70
00:02:23,169 --> 00:02:25,138
I go to the radio show on my own.

71
00:02:25,808 --> 00:02:28,608
I've been working in this industry for 24 years.

72
00:02:29,448 --> 00:02:31,778
But I have no idea how things work at the TV stations.

73
00:02:32,078 --> 00:02:33,448
Starting with the locations,

74
00:02:33,578 --> 00:02:35,298
I don't know where the waiting rooms are...

75
00:02:35,348 --> 00:02:36,417
or how to get to the studios.

76
00:02:36,418 --> 00:02:37,917
- "RS2." "RS3." - That was the biggest reason.

77
00:02:37,918 --> 00:02:39,417
- Sometimes, we confuse the floors. - I worked in this industry...

78
00:02:39,418 --> 00:02:41,088
- Right. - But we come here all the time.

79
00:02:41,488 --> 00:02:43,257
It made me wonder...

80
00:02:43,258 --> 00:02:44,887
if I could proudly say that...

81
00:02:44,888 --> 00:02:46,497
I had been in this industry for 24 years.

82
00:02:46,498 --> 00:02:49,034
So I had been on my own without an agency for a year and a half.

83
00:02:49,058 --> 00:02:51,868
Then I have gotten used to doing things on my own.

84
00:02:52,968 --> 00:02:55,167
One, two, three, ho

85
00:02:55,168 --> 00:02:57,908
(She's gotten used to getting off work alone now.)

86
00:02:58,868 --> 00:03:01,038
My house! My world.

87
00:03:01,308 --> 00:03:02,907
That's part of my routine too. When I'm home, I say,

88
00:03:02,908 --> 00:03:05,578
- "My house. My world." - "My house. My world."

89
00:03:06,478 --> 00:03:07,618
My house is my world indeed.

90
00:03:10,088 --> 00:03:14,018
(She arrives in her world by keeping up with her routine.)

91
00:03:16,288 --> 00:03:20,058
(She enters the house while carrying the shoes inside.)

92
00:03:23,998 --> 00:03:25,768
Wait. Why are you bringing in your shoes?

93
00:03:26,098 --> 00:03:27,797
She has to put them back on the rack.

94
00:03:27,798 --> 00:03:29,207
- Back in the case? - Yes.

95
00:03:29,208 --> 00:03:32,537
That's the thing. My babies ought to go back inside their home too.

96
00:03:32,538 --> 00:03:34,037
(The shoes go back into their home too.)

97
00:03:34,038 --> 00:03:35,438
Rest up.

98
00:03:37,508 --> 00:03:40,078
(She comes out to the living room after putting her shoes away.)

99
00:03:40,348 --> 00:03:41,378
Okay.

100
00:03:45,718 --> 00:03:48,518
Doesn't the table kind of look like a scale?

101
00:03:48,788 --> 00:03:50,427
- What? - My gosh.

102
00:03:50,428 --> 00:03:51,827
- Oh, this? - Come on.

103
00:03:51,828 --> 00:03:53,098
Come on. Don't be like that.

104
00:03:53,458 --> 00:03:54,757
(She puts the hat in the steam closet.)

105
00:03:54,758 --> 00:03:55,968
Let me do that first.

106
00:03:56,428 --> 00:03:58,674
- Okay. I should wash up now. - I put my hats in a steam closet.

107
00:03:58,698 --> 00:03:59,737
- You have to. - Same here.

108
00:03:59,738 --> 00:04:01,137
- I put hats and belts in there too. - Yes.

109
00:04:01,138 --> 00:04:02,297
- People say... - Right.

110
00:04:02,298 --> 00:04:03,507
It could ruin the belts, but I do it anyway...

111
00:04:03,508 --> 00:04:05,214
- when I come home. - You must put everything in there.

112
00:04:05,238 --> 00:04:06,338
Okay.

113
00:04:09,448 --> 00:04:11,648
(Opening up)

114
00:04:11,748 --> 00:04:13,717
I must put the clothes I wore...

115
00:04:13,718 --> 00:04:15,398
- in the steam closet right away. - Right.

116
00:04:15,778 --> 00:04:18,247
That makes things convenient. Otherwise, they get wrinkles...

117
00:04:18,248 --> 00:04:20,018
- or smell. - Right.

118
00:04:21,118 --> 00:04:23,988
(Striding)

119
00:04:25,028 --> 00:04:27,198
(She turns on the bright bathroom lights.)

120
00:04:27,628 --> 00:04:29,598
(Reaching down)

121
00:04:30,728 --> 00:04:31,828
All right.

122
00:04:32,498 --> 00:04:33,768
(Tossing them out)

123
00:04:34,038 --> 00:04:35,198
Her house is always clean.

124
00:04:36,668 --> 00:04:39,507
I installed wallpaper sheets in the bathroom.

125
00:04:39,508 --> 00:04:41,008
- Oh, my. - I decorated it myself.

126
00:04:41,308 --> 00:04:42,308
(The bathroom floor is meant to be kept dry.)

127
00:04:42,309 --> 00:04:44,407
But humidity must be really bad for the bathroom.

128
00:04:44,408 --> 00:04:45,747
- It's hard to keep it dry. - That's why...

129
00:04:45,748 --> 00:04:47,148
I always have to wipe the moisture.

130
00:04:48,348 --> 00:04:49,917
- Look how clean her drain is. - It's crazy...

131
00:04:49,918 --> 00:04:51,447
how the silicone still looks that white.

132
00:04:51,448 --> 00:04:52,617
(White silicone caulk)

133
00:04:52,618 --> 00:04:53,717
- Right. - Look how white it is.

134
00:04:53,718 --> 00:04:54,818
- It's white. - Yes.

135
00:04:55,718 --> 00:04:57,727
What? Is that a new toilet?

136
00:04:57,728 --> 00:05:00,058
(She maintains her bathroom in pristine condition.)

137
00:05:01,498 --> 00:05:04,168
(She takes something out with a rustling sound.)

138
00:05:06,168 --> 00:05:07,438
- What is that? - What is it?

139
00:05:10,638 --> 00:05:12,607
(Spreading it out)

140
00:05:12,608 --> 00:05:13,677
It pops up.

141
00:05:13,678 --> 00:05:14,918
- Is that a tent? - What is it?

142
00:05:14,978 --> 00:05:16,578
- Is that a hat? - What is it?

143
00:05:18,778 --> 00:05:19,847
(Let me see.)

144
00:05:19,848 --> 00:05:21,088
Are you going to dye your hair?

145
00:05:22,218 --> 00:05:24,948
(She takes a mysterious bag next.)

146
00:05:25,418 --> 00:05:28,188
Let me do this first and then wash up.

147
00:05:30,058 --> 00:05:32,928
(Tying her hair)

148
00:05:34,328 --> 00:05:37,028
(She ties up her hair in perfect pigtails.)

149
00:05:38,268 --> 00:05:40,698
(Grabbing)

150
00:05:43,808 --> 00:05:47,077
(She puts it right over her head.)

151
00:05:47,078 --> 00:05:49,777
I know. Parents use that when they wash their kids' hair.

152
00:05:49,778 --> 00:05:52,147
- Right. But that's the adult size. - Really?

153
00:05:52,148 --> 00:05:53,417
- That's the adult size? - Yes.

154
00:05:53,418 --> 00:05:55,658
It looks like a dog cone they wear after being neutered.

155
00:05:55,878 --> 00:05:57,317
It looks like a dog cone they wear after being neutered.

156
00:05:57,318 --> 00:05:58,687
- What? - To prevent the hair from falling.

157
00:05:58,688 --> 00:06:00,918
- Like the neck collar? - Hold on.

158
00:06:01,318 --> 00:06:02,727
- I mean... - What's the point...

159
00:06:02,728 --> 00:06:04,127
of my getting neutered now?

160
00:06:04,128 --> 00:06:05,928
(Apologetic)

161
00:06:06,028 --> 00:06:07,427
It's better to do it early...

162
00:06:07,428 --> 00:06:08,908
- if you plan to get it. - Of course.

163
00:06:09,228 --> 00:06:10,527
- Why do I want to give her treats? - It's not like...

164
00:06:10,528 --> 00:06:12,297
- Like cat treats? - I have a long tongue.

165
00:06:12,298 --> 00:06:14,018
- I don't want any treats from you. - Okay.

166
00:06:14,338 --> 00:06:15,597
- I'm sorry. - They're fishy.

167
00:06:15,598 --> 00:06:16,867
They're fishy.

168
00:06:16,868 --> 00:06:18,438
(My Ae Ong loves them.)

169
00:06:19,808 --> 00:06:22,138
(She puts on the haircut cape, the kind meant for humans.)

170
00:06:24,348 --> 00:06:27,518
(Then she takes something out from a resealable bag.)

171
00:06:28,448 --> 00:06:29,648
- What? - A hair clipper?

172
00:06:29,718 --> 00:06:30,747
Yes.

173
00:06:30,748 --> 00:06:31,818
It's good.

174
00:06:32,388 --> 00:06:34,217
(She nonchalantly turns it on.)

175
00:06:34,218 --> 00:06:36,257
(She starts trimming her hair then.)

176
00:06:36,258 --> 00:06:37,358
Gosh, it's so messy.

177
00:06:37,888 --> 00:06:39,657
(Trimming her hair skillfully)

178
00:06:39,658 --> 00:06:41,697
- Gosh, she doesn't even hesitate. - That can't be easy.

179
00:06:41,698 --> 00:06:42,767
Do you cut your own hair?

180
00:06:42,768 --> 00:06:44,498
- I didn't know she did. - Yes.

181
00:06:44,798 --> 00:06:46,368
Even I can't handle hair clippers.

182
00:06:46,838 --> 00:06:48,267
- He uses scissors. - Really? Scissors?

183
00:06:48,268 --> 00:06:49,737
I've cut my hair with scissors for a long time.

184
00:06:49,738 --> 00:06:50,907
With kitchen scissors.

185
00:06:50,908 --> 00:06:52,107
(HairClipper83 surpasses...)

186
00:06:52,108 --> 00:06:55,878
(Scissors84.)

187
00:06:56,278 --> 00:06:58,808
I've been cutting my own hair for ten years now.

188
00:06:59,178 --> 00:07:01,618
If you look at my hair, you'll see that my hair is thick.

189
00:07:01,878 --> 00:07:03,518
If I grow out the back of my hair,

190
00:07:03,718 --> 00:07:05,617
it will puff up like the character in "The Smoggies."

191
00:07:05,618 --> 00:07:06,788
- Like that. - I see.

192
00:07:07,818 --> 00:07:09,687
At first, I diligently went...

193
00:07:09,688 --> 00:07:11,728
to a hair salon in Gangnam from Mapo.

194
00:07:12,228 --> 00:07:13,357
But I couldn't keep up.

195
00:07:13,358 --> 00:07:15,158
- It's a hassle. - It was such a hassle.

196
00:07:15,528 --> 00:07:16,597
- It's inefficient too. - Yes.

197
00:07:16,598 --> 00:07:18,804
- A round trip would be two hours. - That's a lot of work.

198
00:07:18,828 --> 00:07:20,938
So I decided to learn the skill.

199
00:07:21,038 --> 00:07:25,038
At first, I cut my hair with a dog grooming clipper.

200
00:07:25,338 --> 00:07:27,058
But I ended up shaving too much of my hair.

201
00:07:27,308 --> 00:07:30,948
The back of my head looked bald like a groomed Maltese.

202
00:07:31,978 --> 00:07:33,617
- That's how my hair looked. - A lot of hair gets shaved...

203
00:07:33,618 --> 00:07:34,794
like that with a dog grooming clipper.

204
00:07:34,818 --> 00:07:36,948
- It shaved all of my hair. - Right.

205
00:07:37,788 --> 00:07:39,587
I thought if I kept using the clipper,

206
00:07:39,588 --> 00:07:41,618
my skin would get irritated.

207
00:07:41,718 --> 00:07:43,728
So I started to try out...

208
00:07:43,988 --> 00:07:45,827
several proper hair clippers.

209
00:07:45,828 --> 00:07:48,128
I can't look at the back of my head.

210
00:07:48,558 --> 00:07:50,628
So I feel my hair with my fingers.

211
00:07:50,868 --> 00:07:53,797
- That's how I cut it. - I didn't know you could do that.

212
00:07:53,798 --> 00:07:57,238
If my hair looks too crooked, I can stop by a hair salon...

213
00:07:57,568 --> 00:08:00,337
and get it trimmed again when I go out for work.

214
00:08:00,338 --> 00:08:02,078
(She stops by a hair salon for a trim.)

215
00:08:03,078 --> 00:08:05,908
(Whirring)

216
00:08:07,348 --> 00:08:09,318
Gosh, hair clippers are hard to handle.

217
00:08:10,718 --> 00:08:12,147
You stop it with your fingers.

218
00:08:12,148 --> 00:08:13,908
- So the clipper doesn't go higher. - Right.

219
00:08:16,228 --> 00:08:18,658
Wait. How come my face isn't showing?

220
00:08:18,988 --> 00:08:20,957
I'm sorry, but my belly looks really bulging in this shot.

221
00:08:20,958 --> 00:08:22,457
- That's all we can see. - Wait.

222
00:08:22,458 --> 00:08:24,858
(I'm sorry, but my belly looks really bulging in this shot.)

223
00:08:27,068 --> 00:08:30,307
(As she shaves the back of her head without hesitation, )

224
00:08:30,308 --> 00:08:32,407
(her hair at the back of her head slowly disappears.)

225
00:08:32,408 --> 00:08:34,308
- Oh, my. - She looks like she's enlisting.

226
00:08:37,848 --> 00:08:41,047
(Like a recruit who has left home to enlist, )

227
00:08:41,048 --> 00:08:44,348
(she mercilessly shaves the back of her head.)

228
00:08:50,058 --> 00:08:53,198
(A clear line-up)

229
00:08:55,098 --> 00:08:56,768
(Did I do a good job?)

230
00:08:57,798 --> 00:09:00,837
(Checking herself in the mirror)

231
00:09:00,838 --> 00:09:01,938
It looks good.

232
00:09:05,508 --> 00:09:07,008
- Gosh. - It feels nice.

233
00:09:07,208 --> 00:09:08,608
You shaved quite a lot of hair.

234
00:09:09,038 --> 00:09:11,047
- It's a 2 block haircut. - I used a 3mm clipper guard.

235
00:09:11,048 --> 00:09:12,578
How frequently do you cut your hair?

236
00:09:12,808 --> 00:09:14,317
My hair at the back of my head grows so fast.

237
00:09:14,318 --> 00:09:15,777
It grows so fast.

238
00:09:15,778 --> 00:09:18,218
- Right. - I cut it once every three weeks.

239
00:09:18,448 --> 00:09:20,117
I just use a 3mm clipper guard.

240
00:09:20,118 --> 00:09:22,388
- You can see the back of my head. - Right.

241
00:09:22,558 --> 00:09:24,488
If this part looks messy,

242
00:09:24,758 --> 00:09:26,027
I could look unkempt overall.

243
00:09:26,028 --> 00:09:28,028
- You look neat and nice. - I want to look neat.

244
00:09:28,258 --> 00:09:29,567
You don't have to go to the hair salon.

245
00:09:29,568 --> 00:09:31,404
(She takes good care of the hair at the back of her head.)

246
00:09:31,428 --> 00:09:33,738
(She's done with her haircut.)

247
00:09:34,538 --> 00:09:36,968
(Careful)

248
00:09:38,668 --> 00:09:39,677
(Removing her head)

249
00:09:39,678 --> 00:09:40,907
- That's convenient. - Yes.

250
00:09:40,908 --> 00:09:42,268
- It's really convenient. - Right.

251
00:09:42,408 --> 00:09:43,747
- Not to make a mess. - Then...

252
00:09:43,748 --> 00:09:45,007
- you can just throw that out. - Right.

253
00:09:45,008 --> 00:09:46,877
I just have to throw that out.

254
00:09:46,878 --> 00:09:48,218
