(She goes straight to the door.)

516
00:20:14,908 --> 00:20:16,538
- What's going on? - It's open.

517
00:20:17,778 --> 00:20:20,108
(What bag is this?)

518
00:20:20,348 --> 00:20:21,577
She must have ordered food.

519
00:20:21,578 --> 00:20:22,748
She should. She's sick.

520
00:20:26,018 --> 00:20:27,918
(Let me take them out of the bag.)

521
00:20:28,758 --> 00:20:30,958
(A mysterious insulated bag)

522
00:20:32,988 --> 00:20:34,197
- Strawberries. - Strawberries.

523
00:20:34,198 --> 00:20:35,958
(She takes out sweet and sour strawberries.)

524
00:20:37,298 --> 00:20:39,498
(Grabbing the strawberry box)

525
00:20:42,268 --> 00:20:45,538
(She starts washing them immediately.)

526
00:20:46,208 --> 00:20:48,707
I need vitamins to strengthen my immune system.

527
00:20:48,708 --> 00:20:50,108
- I see. Right. - Yes.

528
00:20:51,978 --> 00:20:54,178
(She places the rinsed strawberries in the bowl.)

529
00:20:57,118 --> 00:20:59,947
(She also pops one in her mouth.)

530
00:20:59,948 --> 00:21:01,987
(And she pops in another.)

531
00:21:01,988 --> 00:21:03,657
- But I do the same thing. - Right.

532
00:21:03,658 --> 00:21:05,658
- I can't be patient. - Right. Who can be patient?

533
00:21:06,088 --> 00:21:07,697
My sense of taste started to get dull.

534
00:21:07,698 --> 00:21:09,858
So I had to keep stimulating it with new food.

535
00:21:11,228 --> 00:21:13,668
(She places 1 in the bowl and pops 1 in her mouth.)

536
00:21:14,768 --> 00:21:16,797
(She keeps on eating strawberries while rinsing them.)

537
00:21:16,798 --> 00:21:18,608
So when I was young,

538
00:21:19,008 --> 00:21:21,137
I used to wonder why my mom only gave me the fruits...

539
00:21:21,138 --> 00:21:22,837
- and didn't eat them. - Right.

540
00:21:22,838 --> 00:21:24,438
- Moms eat more fruits than us. - Right.

541
00:21:25,578 --> 00:21:27,077
(He finally finds out his mother's secret.)

542
00:21:27,078 --> 00:21:28,778
She must already have eaten them.

543
00:21:29,178 --> 00:21:30,347
When moms say they're full,

544
00:21:30,348 --> 00:21:31,348
- They're serious. - they're serious.

545
00:21:31,349 --> 00:21:33,217
"Watching you eat makes me full."

546
00:21:33,218 --> 00:21:34,257
(They mean it 100 percent.)

547
00:21:34,258 --> 00:21:35,258
- That's a fact. - Yes.

548
00:21:36,258 --> 00:21:38,588
(After she finishes washing the tasty strawberries, )

549
00:21:40,528 --> 00:21:42,197
(she brings something out.)

550
00:21:42,198 --> 00:21:43,228
What's that?

551
00:21:43,968 --> 00:21:45,598
- That's rice syrup. - Rice syrup.

552
00:21:48,498 --> 00:21:51,208
(Finishing off with an elegant lick)

553
00:21:52,338 --> 00:21:54,778
(She puts it back right away.)

554
00:21:56,538 --> 00:21:59,078
(She takes out the gold spoon.)

555
00:21:59,208 --> 00:22:02,718
(Crushing)

556
00:22:03,178 --> 00:22:04,287
(Crushing mercilessly)

557
00:22:04,288 --> 00:22:05,388
Why is she crushing them?

558
00:22:07,518 --> 00:22:10,428
(As careful as she was during cleaning)

559
00:22:12,388 --> 00:22:13,628
(Sniffling)

560
00:22:14,628 --> 00:22:15,628
(Coughing)

561
00:22:18,668 --> 00:22:21,638
(She sits on the sofa with the crushed strawberries.)

562
00:22:22,368 --> 00:22:25,068
(She mixes them well.)

563
00:22:27,578 --> 00:22:29,038
She eats them right away.

564
00:22:30,348 --> 00:22:33,748
(What's this?)

565
00:22:34,618 --> 00:22:39,218
(Why is she eating strawberries out of a bowl?)

566
00:22:41,188 --> 00:22:42,258
It's medicine.

567
00:22:42,418 --> 00:22:44,028
I don't eat it for taste.

568
00:22:44,758 --> 00:22:46,997
It's a folk remedy that has been passed down...

569
00:22:46,998 --> 00:22:49,197
from my Cheongdo grandma.

570
00:22:49,198 --> 00:22:50,227
- Really? - I see.

571
00:22:50,228 --> 00:22:51,498
- It's true. - I see.

572
00:22:52,168 --> 00:22:53,468
Whenever I caught a cold,

573
00:22:53,738 --> 00:22:55,644
she gave me this so that it'd pass from sweetness.

574
00:22:55,668 --> 00:22:58,038
It has vitamins, sugar,

575
00:22:58,208 --> 00:23:00,608
and throat-strengthening properties.

576
00:23:01,008 --> 00:23:03,238
I eat it without fail when I catch a cold.

577
00:23:03,878 --> 00:23:05,508
It's much tastier than strawberry syrup.

578
00:23:06,108 --> 00:23:07,317
When you catch a cold,

579
00:23:07,318 --> 00:23:08,954
they give you medicine in strawberry syrup flavor.

580
00:23:08,978 --> 00:23:10,447
- You might be onto something. - Of course.

581
00:23:10,448 --> 00:23:12,318
I wondered why it was strawberry-flavored.

582
00:23:12,848 --> 00:23:15,017
To me, it's something like restorative herb medicine.

583
00:23:15,018 --> 00:23:17,538
(To Shin Young, it's something like restorative herb medicine.)

584
00:23:19,158 --> 00:23:21,258
(Slurping)

585
00:23:24,228 --> 00:23:26,467
(Slurping in a satisfying way)

586
00:23:26,468 --> 00:23:27,798
It isn't gomtang, is it?

587
00:23:28,068 --> 00:23:29,068
My goodness.

588
00:23:30,238 --> 00:23:31,467
- I mean... - For goodness' sake.

589
00:23:31,468 --> 00:23:33,168
They're using a clip of him again!

590
00:23:33,438 --> 00:23:34,684
- I mean... - For goodness' sake.

591
00:23:34,708 --> 00:23:36,637
(They're using a clip of him again!)

592
00:23:36,638 --> 00:23:37,778
He appears each time.

593
00:23:39,448 --> 00:23:42,078
(Drinking like it's soup)

594
00:23:44,648 --> 00:23:46,147
(Drinking with her face buried in the bowl)

595
00:23:46,148 --> 00:23:47,668
- She is really enjoying it. - I know.

596
00:23:49,688 --> 00:23:51,828
(She gathers the last bits.)

597
00:23:53,958 --> 00:23:56,118
- It must be delicious. - The last soup must be tasty.

598
00:23:57,768 --> 00:23:59,097
It cures any sickness.

599
00:23:59,098 --> 00:24:00,098
(That was nice.)

600
00:24:01,498 --> 00:24:02,498
Seriously.

601
00:24:02,499 --> 00:24:03,568
(She clears the bowl.)

602
00:24:04,208 --> 00:24:06,638
(After finishing the strawberry medicine, )

603
00:24:07,308 --> 00:24:09,638
(she goes back into the kitchen.)

604
00:24:09,978 --> 00:24:11,048
It was tasty.

605
00:24:11,878 --> 00:24:13,208
(My goodness)

606
00:24:15,378 --> 00:24:17,247
(Even though she is sick, she washes the bowl right away.)

607
00:24:17,248 --> 00:24:18,768
It's best to do the dishes right away.

608
00:24:20,688 --> 00:24:22,158
Omija tea.

609
00:24:24,288 --> 00:24:25,757
(Grabbing a bowl of rice)

610
00:24:25,758 --> 00:24:27,828
What you ate was an appetizer.

611
00:24:28,728 --> 00:24:30,257
(Now comes the real deal.)

612
00:24:30,258 --> 00:24:31,368
Now comes the main dish.

613
00:24:31,768 --> 00:24:33,898
Strawberries are just medicine.

614
00:24:34,438 --> 00:24:36,044
- I took my medicine. - You took a sack of medicine.

615
00:24:36,068 --> 00:24:37,107
Seriously.

616
00:24:37,108 --> 00:24:38,468
(You took a sack of medicine.)

617
00:24:38,668 --> 00:24:39,867
Let's do that.

618
00:24:39,868 --> 00:24:42,408
(She puts it inside the microwave to thaw.)

619
00:24:45,408 --> 00:24:48,218
(She naturally heads over to the fridge next to her.)

620
00:24:49,548 --> 00:24:51,718
(Rummaging)

621
00:24:55,958 --> 00:24:58,758
(Her hands are full of food items.)

622
00:25:00,898 --> 00:25:02,197
- Stir-fried anchovies? - Stir-fried anchovies.

623
00:25:02,198 --> 00:25:03,238
Yes. Stir-fried anchovies.

624
00:25:03,328 --> 00:25:06,298
It's my first time seeing such a big amount of the dish.

625
00:25:06,698 --> 00:25:07,738
I know.

626
00:25:09,168 --> 00:25:10,397
During the holidays,

627
00:25:10,398 --> 00:25:12,337
- you get many nuts as a gift. - That's right.

628
00:25:12,338 --> 00:25:14,107
- We get them as a gift, - Yes.

629
00:25:14,108 --> 00:25:16,337
- but we can't eat them regularly. - We don't eat them.

630
00:25:16,338 --> 00:25:18,047
So I use them for stir-fried anchovies.

631
00:25:18,048 --> 00:25:19,908
Nuts inside stir-fried anchovies are tasty.

632
00:25:21,748 --> 00:25:23,648
(This time, she takes out the thawed rice.)

633
00:25:24,348 --> 00:25:25,787
(She puts it in the metal bowl.)

634
00:25:25,788 --> 00:25:27,418
She puts everything in the metal bowl.

635
00:25:30,488 --> 00:25:32,928
(She opens the gigantic container of stir-fried anchovies...)

636
00:25:33,228 --> 00:25:35,098
(and pours the dish over rice.)

637
00:25:39,628 --> 00:25:42,028
(She mixes the ingredients after adding a lot of anchovies.)

638
00:25:42,168 --> 00:25:44,137
It's half rice, half anchovies.

639
00:25:44,138 --> 00:25:45,308
It'll be tasty as it is.

640
00:25:45,468 --> 00:25:46,737
That's right. You shouldn't add anything else.

641
00:25:46,738 --> 00:25:47,807
I agree. That's perfect.

642
00:25:47,808 --> 00:25:49,848
- That's just right. - Exactly. You use your hands.

643
00:25:51,508 --> 00:25:53,778
(That's good. I'm done mixing the ingredients.)

644
00:25:55,248 --> 00:25:57,448
(Setting up dried laver in a corner)

645
00:25:59,848 --> 00:26:02,757
(Then she covers the anchovy rice...)

646
00:26:02,758 --> 00:26:04,558
(with dried laver.)

647
00:26:06,328 --> 00:26:09,258
(Eating)

648
00:26:12,768 --> 00:26:14,998
- It's tasty. - Stir-fried anchovies must be good.

649
00:26:15,698 --> 00:26:17,708
Since I'm sick, I need to eat rice.

650
00:26:19,438 --> 00:26:21,614
Most people with a throat infection lose their appetite.

651
00:26:21,638 --> 00:26:23,408
You should eat when you're sick.

652
00:26:25,778 --> 00:26:27,647
(Koreans get their energy from rice!)

653
00:26:27,648 --> 00:26:29,548
(Impressed)

654
00:26:31,388 --> 00:26:32,548
It must be good.

655
00:26:33,748 --> 00:26:35,258
(Eating from time to time, )

656
00:26:36,288 --> 00:26:37,587
(Shin Young piles up...)

657
00:26:37,588 --> 00:26:39,958
(her anchovy gimbap.)

658
00:26:42,558 --> 00:26:47,438
(Eating the remaining dried laver)

659
00:26:51,468 --> 00:26:54,578
(She gathers the remaining rice...)

660
00:26:57,348 --> 00:27:00,818
(and eats it in one bite.)

661
00:27:03,648 --> 00:27:06,417
It's unbelievable that she cooks when she is sick.

662
00:27:06,418 --> 00:27:07,418
I know.

663
00:27:07,818 --> 00:27:10,417
So I brought some.

664
00:27:10,418 --> 00:27:11,727
- Are you serious? - Yes.

665
00:27:11,728 --> 00:27:12,728
- Really? - I want to try it.

666
00:27:12,729 --> 00:27:14,097
- I want it. - I brought some.

667
00:27:14,098 --> 00:27:15,197
Really?

668
00:27:15,198 --> 00:27:16,198
- No way. - Thank you.

669
00:27:16,199 --> 00:27:18,097
Hold on. Stay here.

670
00:27:18,098 --> 00:27:19,568
(Stay here.)

671
00:27:20,568 --> 00:27:22,238
(Oh, my!)

672
00:27:22,438 --> 00:27:23,844
- The dried laver is big. - I mean...

673
00:27:23,868 --> 00:27:25,207
- I mean... - It looks so tasty.

674
00:27:25,208 --> 00:27:26,637
I shouldn't have eaten before the shoot.

675
00:27:26,638 --> 00:27:28,007
- No way! - It looks good.

676
00:27:28,008 --> 00:27:29,307
- Once it's mixed... - This is the setup.

677
00:27:29,308 --> 00:27:31,408
- There is instant rice. - This is...

678
00:27:31,678 --> 00:27:33,077
- It looks good. - stir-fried anchovies you saw.

679
00:27:33,078 --> 00:27:34,117
- This is sudden. - It's mine.

680
00:27:34,118 --> 00:27:35,178
It looks tasty.

681
00:27:35,578 --> 00:27:37,548
You stir-fried nuts and anchovies.

682
00:27:37,788 --> 00:27:39,348
I'll feed you guys...

683
00:27:39,688 --> 00:27:41,158
- one at a time. - Will you feed us?

684
00:27:41,458 --> 00:27:42,458
Of course.

685
00:27:42,459 --> 00:27:43,717
(They just need to eat the anchovy gimbap.)

686
00:27:43,718 --> 00:27:46,127
- She is like an auntie. - I know. This is so sudden.

687
00:27:46,128 --> 00:27:48,228
- She'll scold us if we try to help. - I know.

688
00:27:48,528 --> 00:27:49,928
- Exactly. - Stay put.

689
00:27:50,098 --> 00:27:51,927
- We need to stay put. - Don't do anything. Stay put.

690
00:27:51,928 --> 00:27:53,408
- Staying put is helping. - Stay put.

691
00:27:53,798 --> 00:27:55,098
- To one bowl of rice... - Yes.

692
00:27:55,638 --> 00:27:56,897
How much will you add?

693
00:27:56,898 --> 00:27:59,067
When there is one bowl of rice, you should add this much.

694
00:27:59,068 --> 00:28:00,207
- About half? - Yes.

695
00:28:00,208 --> 00:28:01,614
- It smells so good. - You add a lot.

696
00:28:01,638 --> 00:28:02,838
- That's a lot. - Here.

697
00:28:03,008 --> 00:28:05,208
Combined, they'll be the size of a yellow corvina.

698
00:28:06,048 --> 00:28:08,417
- I see more anchovies than rice. - The ratio is 1 to 1.

699
00:28:08,418 --> 00:28:09,948
The ratio is 1 to 1.

700
00:28:10,348 --> 00:28:12,017
- It looks tasty. - We'll get a bite each.

701
00:28:12,018 --> 00:28:13,587
It's nutritious too.

702
00:28:13,588 --> 00:28:14,657
- Yes, it is. - Yes.

703
00:28:14,658 --> 00:28:16,187
(Once it's wrapped in dried laver, it's done.)

704
00:28:16,188 --> 00:28:17,457
- Firstly... - Hyun Moo, you should go first.

705
00:28:17,458 --> 00:28:18,727
- Here. - Hyun Moo, you should go first.

706
00:28:18,728 --> 00:28:20,797
Here. Eat first.

707
00:28:20,798 --> 00:28:22,478
(She delivers it to Moomoo's mouth first.)

708
00:28:24,728 --> 00:28:25,798
Isn't it good?

709
00:28:26,568 --> 00:28:28,538
- I told you so. - How is it?

710
00:28:28,738 --> 00:28:30,014
It's tasty. It isn't very salty.

711
00:28:30,038 --> 00:28:31,067
- I see. - Isn't it very salty?

712
00:28:31,068 --> 00:28:32,068
I like that it isn't very salty.

713
00:28:32,069 --> 00:28:33,949
- It's mildly seasoned. - It's mildly seasoned.

714
00:28:34,178 --> 00:28:35,208
Eat it.

715
00:28:35,438 --> 00:28:37,748
If stir-fried anchovies are too sweet or too salty,

716
00:28:37,848 --> 00:28:39,307
- you get fed up with them. - It's just right.

717
00:28:39,308 --> 00:28:40,878
Open wide. There you go.

718
00:28:42,648 --> 00:28:43,678
It's good.

719
00:28:44,318 --> 00:28:45,888
- It's tasty! - Right?

720
00:28:46,018 --> 00:28:47,758
It's my first time someone fed me this.

721
00:28:47,988 --> 00:28:49,418
- Really? - Right?

722
00:28:49,588 --> 00:28:50,588
No one has done it.

723
00:28:50,589 --> 00:28:52,058
No one has fed me this.

724
00:28:52,428 --> 00:28:53,428
(Here, Bum June.)

725
00:28:53,429 --> 00:28:54,557
(Twitching)

726
00:28:54,558 --> 00:28:55,627
No one has fed me this.

727
00:28:55,628 --> 00:28:56,828
(Opening)

728
00:28:57,158 --> 00:28:58,627
- All right. - I twitched.

729
00:28:58,628 --> 00:28:59,767
- It's tasty. - It's so tasty.

730
00:28:59,768 --> 00:29:01,098
(I thought it was my turn.)

731
00:29:01,538 --> 00:29:03,538
I added a lot.

732
00:29:03,838 --> 00:29:05,538
- It's like making sushi. - Open wide.

733
00:29:06,268 --> 00:29:08,308
- Don't touch it. - Do you want one more?

734
00:29:08,508 --> 00:29:10,008
- Is it tasty? - It's tasty.

735
00:29:11,708 --> 00:29:13,008
- It's so savory. - I know.

736
00:29:14,318 --> 00:29:16,877
You should eat one too. You made it.

737
00:29:16,878 --> 00:29:18,647
Your stir-fried anchovies are the best.

738
00:29:18,648 --> 00:29:20,148
Shin Young, thank you.

739
00:29:20,448 --> 00:29:21,757
- It's tasty. - I enjoyed it.

740
00:29:21,758 --> 00:29:22,878
- I enjoyed it. - Seriously.

741
00:29:24,628 --> 00:29:26,357
Her stir-fried anchovies aren't salty or sweet.

742
00:29:26,358 --> 00:29:28,057
I could eat a pot of rice this way.

743
00:29:28,058 --> 00:29:29,098
It was so tasty.

744
00:29:29,128 --> 00:29:30,928
(It was tasty.)

745
00:29:31,298 --> 00:29:32,767
Your stir-fried anchovies are the tastiest.

746
00:29:32,768 --> 00:29:33,768
- Really? - Yes.

747
00:29:33,769 --> 00:29:35,997
They're perfect when you make a wrap...

748
00:29:35,998 --> 00:29:37,638
- with dried laver. - They're just right.

749
00:29:39,408 --> 00:29:41,208
(Heave-ho)

750
00:29:43,138 --> 00:29:45,948
(She brings the TV into the kitchen to accompany her during a meal.)

751
00:29:46,708 --> 00:29:48,148
(After setting up the TV)

752
00:29:48,848 --> 00:29:50,818
(Entering stealthily)

753
00:29:51,088 --> 00:29:53,348
- It's a new shift worker. - That's right.

754
00:29:53,448 --> 00:29:54,717
I thought it was a ghost.

755
00:29:54,718 --> 00:29:57,088
(Another Shin Young enters.)

756
00:29:57,858 --> 00:30:00,258
(Pressing the remote control)

757
00:30:00,828 --> 00:30:01,957
Lead-off man.

758
00:30:01,958 --> 00:30:04,168
(Even when she is sick, baseball is a must.)

759
00:30:06,028 --> 00:30:07,997
(Is she beginning to cook again?)

760
00:30:07,998 --> 00:30:08,998
There is more.

761
00:30:08,999 --> 00:30:12,608
It's an accompaniment. It isn't a main dish.

762
00:30:12,868 --> 00:30:14,068
(I see!)

763
00:30:14,678 --> 00:30:16,358
She has more ingredients than a snack bar.

764
00:30:16,938 --> 00:30:18,408
Didn't you say that you were sick?

765
00:30:19,008 --> 00:30:20,008
Exactly.

766
00:30:20,348 --> 00:30:21,348
I mean...

767
00:30:21,349 --> 00:30:22,709
(You should eat when you're sick.)

768
00:30:23,778 --> 00:30:25,538
- Stir-fried fishcake? - What will she make?

769
00:30:26,788 --> 00:30:28,318
She is clearing out the sea today.

770
00:30:30,858 --> 00:30:33,688
(That's good.)

771
00:30:35,658 --> 00:30:38,597
(She picks up the remaining fishcake.)

772
00:30:38,598 --> 00:30:40,398
- You should eat it as it is. - That's right.

773
00:30:40,668 --> 00:30:41,997
(She folds it in half.)

774
00:30:41,998 --> 00:30:43,797
- That's it. It's the tastiest. - That's it.

775
00:30:43,798 --> 00:30:44,938
I agree.

776
00:30:45,268 --> 00:30:46,638
Everyone does it.

777
00:30:48,338 --> 00:30:49,738
(Chopping)

778
00:30:52,878 --> 00:30:54,638
- She does that while being sick. - Exactly.

779
00:30:55,348 --> 00:30:56,918
- But she looks happy. - Yes.

780
00:30:57,588 --> 00:30:59,348
Do I have a mole there?

781
00:31:00,288 --> 00:31:01,387
- Hold on. - Where?

782
00:31:01,388 --> 00:31:03,017
- I think it's an anchovy particle. - On my cheek.

783
00:31:03,018 --> 00:31:04,058
I see.

784
00:31:04,928 --> 00:31:06,288
It must be an anchovy eye.

785
00:31:06,888 --> 00:31:07,998
Is it dried laver?

786
00:31:08,828 --> 00:31:10,897
(A dried laver particle landed on her cheek.)

787
00:31:10,898 --> 00:31:11,898
Oh, yes.

788
00:31:12,728 --> 00:31:15,338
(With a mole on her cheek, )

789
00:31:16,598 --> 00:31:19,138
(she finishes chopping the vegetables in no time.)

790
00:31:20,368 --> 00:31:23,508
(This time, she opens a tub of gochujang.)

791
00:31:25,078 --> 00:31:26,708
(Grabbing)

792
00:31:28,278 --> 00:31:30,158
(She scrapes it and adds it to the metal bowl.)

793
00:31:30,648 --> 00:31:32,718
(She eyeball measures the chili powder.)

794
00:31:33,448 --> 00:31:34,957
(Soy sauce, )

795
00:31:34,958 --> 00:31:36,887
(starch syrup, )

796
00:31:36,888 --> 00:31:39,658
(and minced garlic get added.)

797
00:31:39,788 --> 00:31:41,828
- What is she making? - Gochujang, chili powder...

798
00:31:41,898 --> 00:31:43,157
- Tteokbokki? - Tteokbokki!

799
00:31:43,158 --> 00:31:44,967
- Tteokbokki. - I see.

800
00:31:44,968 --> 00:31:46,404
- It's a tteokbokki sauce. - It's my tteokbokki recipe.

801
00:31:46,428 --> 00:31:48,037
When I was in elementary school,

802
00:31:48,038 --> 00:31:50,597
an auntie sold tteokbokki across from the school.

803
00:31:50,598 --> 00:31:52,037
When she quit,

804
00:31:52,038 --> 00:31:54,198
she gave me the recipe since I ate so much tteokbokki.

805
00:31:54,338 --> 00:31:55,807
- She gave you the recipe. - "Add this and that..."

806
00:31:55,808 --> 00:31:57,237
- "at home." - She gave you the recipe.

807
00:31:57,238 --> 00:31:59,008
- Do you still use that recipe? - Yes.

808
00:32:01,948 --> 00:32:03,318
(Sucking)

809
00:32:03,618 --> 00:32:04,947
(It's perfect.)

810
00:32:04,948 --> 00:32:06,088
Nice.

811
00:32:07,218 --> 00:32:08,488
It's so tasty.

812
00:32:08,558 --> 00:32:10,018
It'll be the talk of the town.

813
00:32:10,388 --> 00:32:11,487
When you're sick,

814
00:32:11,488 --> 00:32:12,787
- you need to eat spicy food. - Right.

815
00:32:12,788 --> 00:32:15,328
- It makes you sweat. - Sweating helps.

816
00:32:16,828 --> 00:32:21,738
(The chopped vegetables go into the pot first.)

817
00:32:22,868 --> 00:32:25,707
(Then she mixes in the sauce.)

818
00:32:25,708 --> 00:32:28,577
You cook like you're at a restaurant even though you're at home.

819
00:32:28,578 --> 00:32:29,808
- Yes. - Right?

820
00:32:31,008 --> 00:32:32,607
(While flavors seep into the vegetable broth)

821
00:32:32,608 --> 00:32:33,678
It looks so tasty.

822
00:32:36,078 --> 00:32:38,188
(Cutting)

823
00:32:39,318 --> 00:32:43,318
(She prepares the main ingredient, rice cake, this time.)

824
00:32:43,588 --> 00:32:45,058
Let's see.

825
00:32:45,758 --> 00:32:46,887
(Long)

826
00:32:46,888 --> 00:32:48,228
- They're so long. - Yes.

827
00:32:49,658 --> 00:32:51,468
It's my specialty.

828
00:32:51,898 --> 00:32:54,567
People slurp noodles, but not tteokbokki.

829
00:32:54,568 --> 00:32:56,938
But I slice all the ingredients into long strips...

830
00:32:57,098 --> 00:32:58,808
so that I can eat them in one bite.

831
00:32:59,038 --> 00:33:00,738
- Will you slurp the fishcake? - Yes.

832
00:33:01,178 --> 00:33:03,408
At first, I used regular wheat flour rice cake.

833
00:33:03,608 --> 00:33:05,208
Then I began cutting the pieces in half.

834
00:33:06,078 --> 00:33:07,438
I cut them so that they'd be long.

835
00:33:07,508 --> 00:33:10,817
But recently, I found out about the long rice cake.

836
00:33:10,818 --> 00:33:12,388
It was a eureka moment.

837
00:33:12,848 --> 00:33:14,888
I must slurp for every meal.

838
00:33:15,588 --> 00:33:18,888
That's my routine for living right.

839
00:33:19,288 --> 00:33:20,627
I must slurp for every meal.

840
00:33:20,628 --> 00:33:21,728
It's a great saying.

841
00:33:23,498 --> 00:33:25,128
(Rinsing)

842
00:33:25,828 --> 00:33:29,068
(She rinses the long wheat flour rice cake.)

843
00:33:30,038 --> 00:33:31,837
I should've done that.

844
00:33:31,838 --> 00:33:33,608
(She adds the long fishcake she has sliced.)

845
00:33:35,778 --> 00:33:37,207
(It looks delicious already.)

846
00:33:37,208 --> 00:33:38,307
It looks good.

847
00:33:38,308 --> 00:33:40,378
I didn't know you could get that color at home.

848
00:33:40,478 --> 00:33:43,318
You get that color when you use rice syrup.

849
00:33:43,578 --> 00:33:47,217
It would be nice with the anchovy gimbap.

850
00:33:47,218 --> 00:33:48,587
- Yes. It's the best combination. - It would be amazing.

851
00:33:48,588 --> 00:33:50,617
- She left some behind for that. - That's right.

852
00:33:50,618 --> 00:33:52,687
But it isn't a leftover. It's what I prepared.

853
00:33:52,688 --> 00:33:55,128
(It isn't a leftover. It's what I prepared.)

854
00:33:55,328 --> 00:33:56,397
- Really? - Yes.

855
00:33:56,398 --> 00:33:59,128
- It isn't a leftover. No. - I thought you were done eating.

856
00:33:59,398 --> 00:34:01,367
I simply ate as I made the dish.

857
00:34:01,368 --> 00:34:04,908
I see why moms can't lose weight.

858
00:34:05,408 --> 00:34:06,508
Moms do that.

859
00:34:07,238 --> 00:34:08,937
- That's so funny. - It's a secret.

860
00:34:08,938 --> 00:34:10,008
I see.

861
00:34:11,308 --> 00:34:13,078
(Opening)

862
00:34:15,778 --> 00:34:16,878
What's that?

863
00:34:17,648 --> 00:34:19,818
(A familiar-looking container?)

864
00:34:20,818 --> 00:34:22,817
The treasure box of my heart.

865
00:34:22,818 --> 00:34:24,527
- I see. Glass noodle container? - Glass noodles.

866
00:34:24,528 --> 00:34:25,988
Yes. It's a glass noodle container.

867
00:34:26,458 --> 00:34:27,897
- Will you add glass noodles again? - A glass noodle container.

868
00:34:27,898 --> 00:34:29,728
(She eats glass noodles for every meal.)

869
00:34:30,328 --> 00:34:33,828
(I guess she adds them whenever the dish has some soup.)

870
00:34:35,338 --> 00:34:36,397
(Glass noodles are a must for the soupy tteokbokki.)

871
00:34:36,398 --> 00:34:39,407
She couldn't hold back upon seeing the soup.

872
00:34:39,408 --> 00:34:40,568
They're essential.

873
00:34:41,538 --> 00:34:43,308
(Opening)

874
00:34:43,978 --> 00:34:45,077
(Shin Young's soaked jewels)

875
00:34:45,078 --> 00:34:46,978
Look at the soaked glass noodles. How detailed.

876
00:34:48,018 --> 00:34:50,448
(She carefully removes the water.)

877
00:34:52,718 --> 00:34:54,958
(She adds a handful of glass noodles.)

878
00:34:55,818 --> 00:34:58,957
(Lastly, it's time to add the rice cake.)

879
00:34:58,958 --> 00:35:00,328
Let's add the rice cake.

880
00:35:00,558 --> 00:35:02,297
You aren't watching baseball today as always.

881
00:35:02,298 --> 00:35:04,358
- I'm watching. I'm listening. - Are you listening?

882
00:35:05,328 --> 00:35:07,837
(Sucking in a breath)

883
00:35:07,838 --> 00:35:09,898
(I'm salivating.)

884
00:35:10,268 --> 00:35:11,707
It's done. It's finished.

885
00:35:11,708 --> 00:35:14,107
(Shin Young's long tteokbokki with glass noodles is complete.)

886
00:35:14,108 --> 00:35:16,108
- Look at that. - It makes me clap.

887
00:35:16,578 --> 00:35:18,978
I wish there were a snack bar that sold the same tteokbokki.

888
00:35:19,208 --> 00:35:20,507
Come to my place.

889
00:35:20,508 --> 00:35:23,377
I won't go.

890
00:35:23,378 --> 00:35:24,418
(Feeling pressured)

891
00:35:25,048 --> 00:35:28,758
I don't care about pooping or creating a mess.

892
00:35:29,088 --> 00:35:31,057
I clean up when the guests leave.

893
00:35:31,058 --> 00:35:33,758
- I don't make the guests... - But I'll worry about it.

894
00:35:34,528 --> 00:35:36,457
- Her house will be like torture. - Why?

895
00:35:36,458 --> 00:35:38,397
You're bound to poop when you eat that much.

896
00:35:38,398 --> 00:35:40,358
- I'll poop at a shopping center. - That's right.

897
00:35:40,668 --> 00:35:43,768
- I'll feel so bad on my way home. - Seriously.

898
00:35:46,268 --> 00:35:48,538
Since I'm sick, I'll eat a bit more.

899
00:35:50,408 --> 00:35:54,077
(Since she is sick, she takes one handful.)

900
00:35:54,078 --> 00:35:56,778
(She takes two handfuls.)

901
00:35:56,978 --> 00:35:58,317
I'll get some rice cake.

902
00:35:58,318 --> 00:35:59,517
(The third handful is the last one.)

903
00:35:59,518 --> 00:36:00,687
That's a lot.

904
00:36:00,688 --> 00:36:02,128
(The third handful is the last one.)

905
00:36:02,888 --> 00:36:05,728
(This is enough.)

906
00:36:07,058 --> 00:36:08,457
- She adds pepper even in there. - That's right.

907
00:36:08,458 --> 00:36:09,458
(Sprinkling pepper)

908
00:36:10,358 --> 00:36:11,467
That's right.

909
00:36:11,468 --> 00:36:13,298
- That's incredible. - Seriously.

910
00:36:14,268 --> 00:36:15,337
You see that color in tteokbokki...

911
00:36:15,338 --> 00:36:16,767
- only in front of a girls' high. - That's right.

912
00:36:16,768 --> 00:36:18,644
- You're right. Not a boys' high. - Definitely not a boys' high.

913
00:36:18,668 --> 00:36:19,738
Boys aren't picky.

914
00:36:21,578 --> 00:36:22,678
That's right. I agree.

915
00:36:24,308 --> 00:36:27,348
(Humming)

916
00:36:28,378 --> 00:36:31,348
(She takes out another plate.)

917
00:36:32,048 --> 00:36:33,118
All right.

918
00:36:33,648 --> 00:36:34,757
- Pickled radish. - There is so much.

919
00:36:34,758 --> 00:36:36,757
- Why are you getting so much? - It's a whole plate.

920
00:36:36,758 --> 00:36:38,388
She emptied the container.

921
00:36:40,428 --> 00:36:41,527
All right.

922
00:36:41,528 --> 00:36:44,568
(She rushes over to eat.)

923
00:36:47,128 --> 00:36:50,098
(She takes off her glasses to begin eating in earnest.)

924
00:36:51,808 --> 00:36:52,808
(Blowing)

925
00:36:54,578 --> 00:36:56,207
(Slurping)

926
00:36:56,208 --> 00:36:57,308
How nice.

927
00:36:58,078 --> 00:36:59,108
It looks tasty.

928
00:36:59,678 --> 00:37:03,048
(She picks up the rice cake, fishcake, and glass noodles.)

929
00:37:03,148 --> 00:37:07,988
(She slurps the three ingredients.)

930
00:37:10,418 --> 00:37:11,558
It's tasty.

931
00:37:12,828 --> 00:37:15,358
(Her eyes go wide.)

932
00:37:16,158 --> 00:37:17,958
- You aren't crying, are you? - How touching.

933
00:37:18,298 --> 00:37:19,668
It made me cry.

934
00:37:21,368 --> 00:37:22,368
(Slurping)

935
00:37:23,298 --> 00:37:25,267
The sound is insane.

936
00:37:25,268 --> 00:37:28,577
- It looks so tasty. - It looks unbelievably tasty.

937
00:37:28,578 --> 00:37:29,854
(She inhales the food without missing anything.)

938
00:37:29,878 --> 00:37:31,777
(Ecstatic)

939
00:37:31,778 --> 00:37:32,848
Look at that.

940
00:37:32,978 --> 00:37:34,777
(Shaking her head)

941
00:37:34,778 --> 00:37:37,117
- Look at that. - Are you gnawing on a rib?

942
00:37:37,118 --> 00:37:38,587
- Hold on. What's that? - She is a lion.

943
00:37:38,588 --> 00:37:41,258
Am I a seal or what? Hold on.

944
00:37:41,388 --> 00:37:43,288
It's so funny. You eat like this.

945
00:37:43,458 --> 00:37:46,328
- You're like a seal. - Like someone who was never sick.

946
00:37:47,758 --> 00:37:49,357
Gosh, it's spicy.

947
00:37:49,358 --> 00:37:50,658
(She restores her energy fully.)

948
00:37:51,368 --> 00:37:54,367
Let's put pickled radish on the top.

949
00:37:54,368 --> 00:37:56,138
(She puts pickled radish on the top.)

950
00:37:58,908 --> 00:38:01,137
(My goodness)

951
00:38:01,138 --> 00:38:03,278
- I love the thin pickled radish. - That's right.

952
00:38:03,678 --> 00:38:05,278
- You know what's good, Bum June. - Yes.

953
00:38:07,478 --> 00:38:08,947
My nose is runny.

954
00:38:08,948 --> 00:38:10,018
(Grabbing)

955
00:38:11,248 --> 00:38:15,518
(Sweat rolls down her face.)

956
00:38:16,618 --> 00:38:19,258
Invigorating food is what you enjoy.

957
00:38:19,528 --> 00:38:22,098
It's what makes you sweat.

958
00:38:22,298 --> 00:38:24,398
People's idea of invigorating food is...

959
00:38:24,528 --> 00:38:27,127
duck meat. It's tasty.

960
00:38:27,128 --> 00:38:29,398
Samgyetang is tasty as well. All of those are tasty.

961
00:38:29,538 --> 00:38:32,168
But I must add glass noodles. I must eat them once a day.

962
00:38:32,668 --> 00:38:34,338
I must slurp them.

963
00:38:34,538 --> 00:38:36,938
Invigorating food is what you enjoy the most. Seriously.

964
00:38:38,508 --> 00:38:39,978
(Slurping fast)

965
00:38:40,948 --> 00:38:44,817
(She becomes absorbed in eating her invigorating food.)

966
00:38:44,818 --> 00:38:46,178
Watch the baseball game, will you?

967
00:38:46,948 --> 00:38:48,308
Watch the baseball game, will you?

968
00:38:50,018 --> 00:38:51,827
(I forgot about that.)

969
00:38:51,828 --> 00:38:54,057
- You didn't watch for a second. - I listened.

970
00:38:54,058 --> 00:38:55,497
- I watched like this. - Don't be ridiculous.

971
00:38:55,498 --> 00:38:56,657
- Last time, - I watched like this.

972
00:38:56,658 --> 00:38:57,827
She was self-conscious enough...

973
00:38:57,828 --> 00:39:00,167
to glance over at the TV as she put food in her mouth.

974
00:39:00,168 --> 00:39:01,344
She isn't even listening this time.

975
00:39:01,368 --> 00:39:02,888
- I'm watching the game. - Not at all.

976
00:39:05,038 --> 00:39:06,958
She won't notice it if someone turns off the TV.

977
00:39:07,668 --> 00:39:09,808
- I'm watching the game. - For goodness' sake.

978
00:39:12,778 --> 00:39:14,277
- This is insane. - Also,

979
00:39:14,278 --> 00:39:16,417
there is the anchovy gimbap.

980
00:39:16,418 --> 00:39:18,418
- It's the best. - It should be eaten together.

981
00:39:19,388 --> 00:39:22,688
(She eats it in one go.)

982
00:39:22,958 --> 00:39:24,488
It looks so tasty.

983
00:39:26,928 --> 00:39:30,698
(This is nice.)

984
00:39:31,398 --> 00:39:33,498
(Wiping the table)

985
00:39:39,508 --> 00:39:42,778
(She pushes food around instead of eating.)

986
00:39:43,008 --> 00:39:44,438
Gosh, it's spicy.

987
00:39:45,478 --> 00:39:46,647
It's a bit spicy.

988
00:39:46,648 --> 00:39:48,378
(Why is she getting up?)

989
00:39:49,748 --> 00:39:50,878
Will she get more?

990
00:39:51,948 --> 00:39:53,788
With the excuse of the food being too spicy...

991
00:39:53,918 --> 00:39:55,418
She'll add something.

992
00:39:58,058 --> 00:39:59,157
I'll eat more later.

993
00:39:59,158 --> 00:40:00,558
(To be continued)

994
00:40:00,688 --> 00:40:04,128
(Is Shin Young leaving food behind?)

995
00:40:04,934 --> 00:40:06,034
I'll eat more later.

996
00:40:07,934 --> 00:40:09,643
I stopped then and there.

997
00:40:09,644 --> 00:40:11,444
- You know how to stop. - I left food behind.

998
00:40:12,074 --> 00:40:15,844
(The glass noodle factory stops running for the first time.)

999
00:40:16,714 --> 00:40:19,654
(Feeling troubled)

1000
00:40:20,154 --> 00:40:22,454
This happens maybe three times a year.

1001
00:40:23,184 --> 00:40:24,524
When I have a cold...

1002
00:40:25,194 --> 00:40:28,064
with a runny nose or bronchitis,

1003
00:40:28,394 --> 00:40:29,564
I can't taste the flavors.

1004
00:40:29,894 --> 00:40:31,364
At first, the food is tasty.

1005
00:40:31,694 --> 00:40:33,934
But the fever makes the inside of the nose swell.

1006
00:40:34,364 --> 00:40:36,364
When that happens, I can't taste anything.

1007
00:40:36,534 --> 00:40:37,854
That's when I put down the spoon.

1008
00:40:38,074 --> 00:40:39,504
I do it with determination.

1009
00:40:40,204 --> 00:40:41,304
I do it with determination.

1010
00:40:42,444 --> 00:40:45,974
When my nose is stuffy, I can't taste the food.

1011
00:40:46,444 --> 00:40:49,644
But you've eaten enough.

1012
00:40:49,984 --> 00:40:51,043
(Really?)

1013
00:40:51,044 --> 00:40:52,384
You ate strawberries too.

1014
00:40:53,114 --> 00:40:54,853
(Despite having swollen nasal passages, )

1015
00:40:54,854 --> 00:40:56,624
(she eats enough and goes to the sink.)

1016
00:40:57,954 --> 00:40:59,053
She is neat.

1017
00:40:59,054 --> 00:41:01,153
(She cleans up right away even when she is sick.)

1018
00:41:01,154 --> 00:41:02,393
Shin Young never throws food out.

1019
00:41:02,394 --> 00:41:03,794
I never throw food out.

1020
00:41:06,634 --> 00:41:07,664
Let's see.

1021
00:41:10,834 --> 00:41:12,374
(Sighing)

1022
00:41:12,734 --> 00:41:13,734
(The side dish container is way up there.)

1023
00:41:13,735 --> 00:41:17,143
I had to put in the leftover tteokbokki,

1024
00:41:17,144 --> 00:41:18,673
but it was way up there.

1025
00:41:18,674 --> 00:41:21,344
I see. You must've never had any leftovers until now.

1026
00:41:23,714 --> 00:41:26,053
(Let's go up.)

1027
00:41:26,054 --> 00:41:27,054
Heave-ho!

1028
00:41:27,055 --> 00:41:28,384
(Slipping)

1029
00:41:28,454 --> 00:41:29,454
Heave-ho!

1030
00:41:30,054 --> 00:41:31,223
Gosh, I almost died.

1031
00:41:31,224 --> 00:41:33,694
- That moment... - Gosh, my shin hurts!

1032
00:41:34,724 --> 00:41:36,464
- Gosh! - Gosh, I almost died.

1033
00:41:37,424 --> 00:41:40,494
- She stopped herself from cursing. - "I almost died."

1034
00:41:41,094 --> 00:41:43,534
It was just a groan.

1035
00:41:45,604 --> 00:41:47,933
