1100
00:44:55,264 --> 00:44:57,564
- Why the metal bowl? - Why does it keep appearing?

1101
00:44:58,164 --> 00:44:59,633
You're eating with the metal bowl all day long!

1102
00:44:59,634 --> 00:45:01,533
How many metal bowls do you have?

1103
00:45:01,534 --> 00:45:03,764
You might develop hyperlipidemia! Be careful.

1104
00:45:06,634 --> 00:45:07,973
The whole bowl is taken out?

1105
00:45:07,974 --> 00:45:09,204
No!

1106
00:45:10,274 --> 00:45:11,973
That's high in calories.

1107
00:45:11,974 --> 00:45:13,694
(The whole bowl of ice cream is taken out.)

1108
00:45:14,714 --> 00:45:16,884
When one gets tonsillitis...

1109
00:45:17,544 --> 00:45:19,153
or a cold,

1110
00:45:19,154 --> 00:45:20,584
mothers give ice cream.

1111
00:45:21,214 --> 00:45:22,424
It's for the fever.

1112
00:45:22,484 --> 00:45:24,284
The fever is brought down with the ice cream.

1113
00:45:25,054 --> 00:45:26,154
It's a tonic.

1114
00:45:26,494 --> 00:45:28,323
- That's a no. - It was because I was sick.

1115
00:45:28,324 --> 00:45:29,524
(Being brazen)

1116
00:45:30,424 --> 00:45:32,333
(Shall I start putting together the tonic?)

1117
00:45:32,334 --> 00:45:33,834
(Opening)

1118
00:45:36,764 --> 00:45:39,234
(Potato chips?)

1119
00:45:40,374 --> 00:45:44,104
(Crushing)

1120
00:45:46,744 --> 00:45:48,843
Really? Potato chips on ice cream?

1121
00:45:48,844 --> 00:45:49,883
- It's really good. - Right.

1122
00:45:49,884 --> 00:45:51,004
- It's really good. - Right.

1123
00:45:51,114 --> 00:45:53,614
Gosh, being sick makes me crave these things.

1124
00:45:54,114 --> 00:45:56,083
Won't that scratch up the roof of your mouth?

1125
00:45:56,084 --> 00:45:58,994
No. It's okay, as it was mashed up finely.

1126
00:45:59,154 --> 00:46:01,354
All right. Shall I dig in?

1127
00:46:02,094 --> 00:46:03,334
I will start eating in earnest.

1128
00:46:04,964 --> 00:46:07,594
She's eating really well as someone who is sick.

1129
00:46:07,694 --> 00:46:10,864
I had to feed myself well. Who will take care of me?

1130
00:46:11,504 --> 00:46:14,004
(She takes a bite of the tonic she put together for herself.)

1131
00:46:16,274 --> 00:46:17,274
Gosh.

1132
00:46:20,214 --> 00:46:21,643
(My goodness. This was what I wanted.)

1133
00:46:21,644 --> 00:46:25,044
(Is she sniffling?)

1134
00:46:29,824 --> 00:46:33,454
(She rolls a big scoop with her wrist.)

1135
00:46:34,224 --> 00:46:39,794
(She shoves it in after opening up her throat.)

1136
00:46:44,164 --> 00:46:45,174
It was the best.

1137
00:46:52,314 --> 00:46:53,373
Gosh, it's good.

1138
00:46:53,374 --> 00:46:56,114
(I feel much better.)

1139
00:46:57,214 --> 00:47:00,054
(She scoops another bite with the crunchy potato chips.)

1140
00:47:00,714 --> 00:47:02,653
As it went down my throat,

1141
00:47:02,654 --> 00:47:07,223
it soothed my swollen throat and salivary glands.

1142
00:47:07,224 --> 00:47:09,664
- It brought everything down. - That's right.

1143
00:47:10,324 --> 00:47:11,834
I'm eating it to get better.

1144
00:47:12,294 --> 00:47:14,394
When I have tonsillitis or am feeling sick,

1145
00:47:14,564 --> 00:47:16,433
having something smooth will...

1146
00:47:16,434 --> 00:47:17,464
- That's enough. - Right.

1147
00:47:17,604 --> 00:47:18,933
- I'm serious. - Stop trying to connect...

1148
00:47:18,934 --> 00:47:20,274
to your illness.

1149
00:47:20,304 --> 00:47:21,973
I'm serious! I was actually sick!

1150
00:47:21,974 --> 00:47:23,534
She's saying so many groundless things.

1151
00:47:24,404 --> 00:47:25,414
Gosh.

1152
00:47:26,274 --> 00:47:27,744
My throat doesn't hurt now.

1153
00:47:29,284 --> 00:47:30,913
(She brought down her throat infection...)

1154
00:47:30,914 --> 00:47:32,194
(with half a bowl of ice cream.)

1155
00:47:34,254 --> 00:47:35,824
(Grabbing the tissue)

1156
00:47:42,224 --> 00:47:43,824
(Getting up)

1157
00:47:52,704 --> 00:47:54,174
(Grabbing)

1158
00:47:55,274 --> 00:47:58,613
(She has leftovers again?)

1159
00:47:58,614 --> 00:48:01,844
(She covers it up diligently with the plastic wrap.)

1160
00:48:04,814 --> 00:48:06,683
(It gets stored in the refrigerator just like the tteokbokki.)

1161
00:48:06,684 --> 00:48:09,353
I wasn't able to finish it as I was sick.

1162
00:48:09,354 --> 00:48:10,900
(I wasn't able to finish it as I was sick.)

1163
00:48:10,924 --> 00:48:12,624
(Coughing)

1164
00:48:13,124 --> 00:48:14,124
(Coughing)

1165
00:48:16,564 --> 00:48:18,293
(She takes out a bunch of dried laundry.)

1166
00:48:18,294 --> 00:48:20,063
She gets everything done even though she's sick.

1167
00:48:20,064 --> 00:48:21,463
Things like the laundry...

1168
00:48:21,464 --> 00:48:23,584
- They must be done quickly. - can't get pushed back.

1169
00:48:23,734 --> 00:48:28,504
(I must fold the laundry even though I'm sick.)

1170
00:48:29,674 --> 00:48:31,914
(Heave-ho!)

1171
00:48:34,744 --> 00:48:37,884
(Let's see.)

1172
00:48:39,414 --> 00:48:41,583
(She folds it nicely into three equal parts.)

1173
00:48:41,584 --> 00:48:42,983
Do you fold your socks like that?

1174
00:48:42,984 --> 00:48:44,054
Yes. Always.

1175
00:48:45,154 --> 00:48:47,794
(Throwing into the basket)

1176
00:48:49,264 --> 00:48:50,664
(Sniffling)

1177
00:48:50,764 --> 00:48:52,533
Gosh, the rhinitis looks bad.

1178
00:48:52,534 --> 00:48:54,434
- Right. - Gosh.

1179
00:48:54,764 --> 00:48:56,564
I felt so sick at that time.

1180
00:48:58,004 --> 00:49:00,374
(She folds it neatly even while sniffling.)

1181
00:49:00,504 --> 00:49:02,003
- Like that. - I also fold the towel like that.

1182
00:49:02,004 --> 00:49:03,374
- Right. Like a ball. - Right.

1183
00:49:05,874 --> 00:49:06,874
(Sniffling)

1184
00:49:09,114 --> 00:49:13,814
(She works diligently even when she's in bad condition.)

1185
00:49:15,724 --> 00:49:18,594
(I'm done.)

1186
00:49:22,064 --> 00:49:24,024
(Heave-ho!)

1187
00:49:25,224 --> 00:49:26,833
(The folded laundry gets put back in.)

1188
00:49:26,834 --> 00:49:27,834
Gosh.

1189
00:49:27,834 --> 00:49:28,834
(That's amazing.)

1190
00:49:28,964 --> 00:49:30,864
Gosh, it's like a hotel!

1191
00:49:32,374 --> 00:49:33,933
Gosh, I'm done now.

1192
00:49:33,934 --> 00:49:35,133
You're done now. Get some rest.

1193
00:49:35,134 --> 00:49:37,244
(Coughing)

1194
00:49:39,144 --> 00:49:41,514
(Rustling)

1195
00:49:43,084 --> 00:49:46,814
(She puts a piece of candy into her mouth.)

1196
00:49:48,014 --> 00:49:49,683
(Lying down)

1197
00:49:49,684 --> 00:49:51,754
She's lying down for the first time.

1198
00:49:58,894 --> 00:50:03,264
(She finally lies down after getting the house chores done.)

1199
00:50:05,504 --> 00:50:06,574
Let's watch together.

1200
00:50:08,674 --> 00:50:09,704
How cute.

1201
00:50:10,174 --> 00:50:11,844
They have similar heights.

1202
00:50:12,014 --> 00:50:14,544
(They're just like each other.)

1203
00:50:14,574 --> 00:50:16,114
What are you saying?

1204
00:50:17,414 --> 00:50:21,214
(A sense of comfort from a similar height)

1205
00:50:22,584 --> 00:50:26,324
(She covers herself with a cozy blanket as well.)

1206
00:50:27,324 --> 00:50:28,393
Support my team.

1207
00:50:28,394 --> 00:50:30,564
(Support my team, Wilson.)

1208
00:50:35,134 --> 00:50:36,604
It feels sad to be sick,

1209
00:50:37,634 --> 00:50:39,074
but it feels worse to be lazy.

1210
00:50:39,874 --> 00:50:42,374
There's no need for crying. It's a waste of tissues.

1211
00:50:42,774 --> 00:50:46,814
If I'm focused on feeling pity from my sickness,

1212
00:50:47,614 --> 00:50:50,183
I turn into the most miserable person in the world.

1213
00:50:50,184 --> 00:50:51,584
- Right. - It just feels miserable.

1214
00:50:51,814 --> 00:50:53,154
Who will wash my socks?

1215
00:50:53,384 --> 00:50:55,254
Sad Shin Young has to wash them.

1216
00:50:55,484 --> 00:50:58,454
Instead of being like that, I think realistically now.

1217
00:50:58,994 --> 00:51:00,324
We have to live on.

1218
00:51:00,394 --> 00:51:01,994
We should take medicine if we feel sick.

1219
00:51:02,124 --> 00:51:04,044
We should get an IV drip if we feel really sick.

1220
00:51:04,164 --> 00:51:05,804
We should get an injection on the bottom.

1221
00:51:06,164 --> 00:51:07,964
We must carry on with life.

1222
00:51:08,094 --> 00:51:10,054
Those who feel sad must see things realistically.

1223
00:51:10,604 --> 00:51:13,204
I think it's right about feeling worse to be lazy.

1224
00:51:14,134 --> 00:51:16,404
We've all been through this. When we were students,

1225
00:51:16,904 --> 00:51:19,473
we said, "I feel so sick. May I go to the nurse's office?"

1226
00:51:19,474 --> 00:51:20,920
We went to the nurse's office just like that.

1227
00:51:20,944 --> 00:51:22,013
Let's say I was filming for a show, and I said,

1228
00:51:22,014 --> 00:51:23,334
"May I go to the nurse's office?"

1229
00:51:23,714 --> 00:51:24,744
"Career over."

1230
00:51:25,884 --> 00:51:29,054
"I feel awful. I want to go home."

1231
00:51:29,324 --> 00:51:30,423
"Career over."

1232
00:51:30,424 --> 00:51:31,483
(Career over)

1233
00:51:31,484 --> 00:51:33,423
"She has a crazy personality!"

1234
00:51:33,424 --> 00:51:34,793
"Kim Shin Young leaves during show."

1235
00:51:34,794 --> 00:51:36,870
"Will she be able to carry on?" People will say these things.

1236
00:51:36,894 --> 00:51:39,464
I must be 100 percent responsible for myself.

1237
00:51:39,664 --> 00:51:42,133
Being sick is fine.

1238
00:51:42,134 --> 00:51:43,604
Anyone can get sick.

1239
00:51:43,734 --> 00:51:46,534
Adding in feelings, fantasies,

1240
00:51:46,674 --> 00:51:49,044
and sorrow? There's no time for that.

1241
00:51:49,174 --> 00:51:51,973
Anyone can catch a cold.

1242
00:51:51,974 --> 00:51:53,244
Colds will go away in the end.

1243
00:51:53,444 --> 00:51:55,173
Colds are things that can get treated.

1244
00:51:55,174 --> 00:51:56,243
You will get better.

1245
00:51:56,244 --> 00:51:57,944
I went to see the doctor on Sunday.

1246
00:51:58,144 --> 00:51:59,984
There were 40 people waiting in line after me.

1247
00:52:00,084 --> 00:52:01,184
They were all sick.

1248
00:52:01,514 --> 00:52:02,960
They all came to see the doctor on their own.

1249
00:52:02,984 --> 00:52:05,654
While shedding tears at home alone,

1250
00:52:05,854 --> 00:52:08,153
I can't say, "I feel so sick. Come and see me."

1251
00:52:08,154 --> 00:52:09,440
I can see a doctor instead of doing that.

1252
00:52:09,464 --> 00:52:10,493
Nobody cries at this age.

1253
00:52:10,494 --> 00:52:12,540
Nobody screams their head off while getting a shot on their bottom.

1254
00:52:12,564 --> 00:52:14,094
If I scream at the age of 44,

1255
00:52:14,334 --> 00:52:16,534
people will say, "She's insane. What's wrong with her?"

1256
00:52:16,604 --> 00:52:18,064
"Kim Shin Young is a lunatic."

1257
00:52:18,534 --> 00:52:20,334
"She's screaming her head off."

1258
00:52:20,534 --> 00:52:21,810
Someone will write those kinds of comments. That can't happen.

1259
00:52:21,834 --> 00:52:23,774
I have to endure everything as I'm an adult.

1260
00:52:24,304 --> 00:52:26,343
That's being ridiculous at my age.

1261
00:52:26,344 --> 00:52:27,414
That can't happen.

1262
00:52:27,814 --> 00:52:30,084
I must live gallantly with both feet on the ground.

1263
00:52:30,384 --> 00:52:32,014
I have to stay alert when I feel sick.

1264
00:52:32,384 --> 00:52:34,954
I must grind myself until the end.

1265
00:52:35,154 --> 00:52:36,224
That's impressive.

1266
00:52:36,454 --> 00:52:39,323
I must move to live while I'm feeling sick.

1267
00:52:39,324 --> 00:52:40,994
- Right. - Right.

1268
00:52:43,664 --> 00:52:45,994
(Blinking)

1269
00:52:49,504 --> 00:52:52,274
(Snoring)

1270
00:52:53,234 --> 00:52:59,114
(Shin Young crashes out after the exhausting day.)

1271
00:53:01,014 --> 00:53:02,014
(Gosh!)

1272
00:53:02,015 --> 00:53:03,643
(Embarrassed)

1273
00:53:03,644 --> 00:53:05,244
(Gosh!)

1274
00:53:12,624 --> 00:53:16,424
(She falls asleep again.)

1275
00:53:17,794 --> 00:53:21,893
(Gallantly Riding Out Alone)

1276
00:53:21,894 --> 00:53:23,004
(I Live Alone)

1277
00:53:23,134 --> 00:53:24,304
It's Dowoon.

1278
00:53:24,764 --> 00:53:27,134
All right. Why are you clapping?

1279
00:53:27,304 --> 00:53:28,903
- Sorry? - What was that about?

1280
00:53:28,904 --> 00:53:30,304
What's wrong?

1281
00:53:32,214 --> 00:53:33,214
(Running?)

1282
00:53:33,215 --> 00:53:34,895
(That will never happen again in my life.)

1283
00:53:35,844 --> 00:53:38,853
(Dowoon left a significant message after the Fun Run.)

1284
00:53:38,854 --> 00:53:40,014
I had a lot of fun.

1285
00:53:40,884 --> 00:53:42,554
- What was that about? - What's wrong?

1286
00:53:43,224 --> 00:53:44,653
Where would I go?

1287
00:53:44,654 --> 00:53:45,694
- Are you sure? - Yes.

1288
00:53:45,924 --> 00:53:47,624
The Fun Run was amazing!

1289
00:53:48,424 --> 00:53:49,623
"The Fun Run was amazing!"

1290
00:53:49,624 --> 00:53:51,824
That can be his last Fun Run.

1291
00:53:52,064 --> 00:53:53,493
I'm planning to make him come for a real run.

1292
00:53:53,494 --> 00:53:54,693
He will never do a real run.

1293
00:53:54,694 --> 00:53:56,333
What do you think about a real run?

1294
00:53:56,334 --> 00:53:57,563
I love both of them.

1295
00:53:57,564 --> 00:53:59,004
Running is just...

1296
00:53:59,404 --> 00:54:00,533
(Smirking)

1297
00:54:00,534 --> 00:54:02,373
Dowoon is more toward my side.

1298
00:54:02,374 --> 00:54:04,604
Dowoon and Na Ra are more toward my side.

1299
00:54:04,804 --> 00:54:06,174
I won't try to take Na Ra.

1300
00:54:06,314 --> 00:54:07,773
- Just... - Why are you trying to take Dowoon?

1301
00:54:07,774 --> 00:54:08,884
Let Dowoon come to my side.

1302
00:54:09,044 --> 00:54:10,943
- He's trying to go against us. - That's not it.

1303
00:54:10,944 --> 00:54:13,353
I have to show people the joy of a real run.

1304
00:54:13,354 --> 00:54:15,553
The Fun Run has a lot more content.

1305
00:54:15,554 --> 00:54:16,684
Right.

1306
00:54:17,254 --> 00:54:19,293
There's food, traveling,

1307
00:54:19,294 --> 00:54:21,053
- You've really chosen that path. - and there's talking.

1308
00:54:21,054 --> 00:54:22,054
I would join the Fun Run as well.

1309
00:54:22,055 --> 00:54:23,593
There's drawing as well.

1310
00:54:23,594 --> 00:54:25,634
- The real run is just running. - Right.

1311
00:54:25,664 --> 00:54:26,944
It's just about setting records.

1312
00:54:28,094 --> 00:54:29,334
I should get myself prepared.

1313
00:54:29,904 --> 00:54:32,584
All right. Here's a member who is about to join the second Fun Run.

1314
00:54:32,874 --> 00:54:34,473
- Let's watch Joy's clip. - The Fun Run?

1315
00:54:34,474 --> 00:54:36,003
(Let's watch Joy's clip.)

1316
00:54:36,004 --> 00:54:37,484
He relates everything to the Fun Run.

1317
00:54:38,674 --> 00:54:40,413
(Enjoy the New Journey!)

1318
00:54:40,414 --> 00:54:41,714
- "Enjoy!" - "Enjoy!"

1319
00:54:45,414 --> 00:54:47,753
(Joy heads somewhere.)

1320
00:54:47,754 --> 00:54:49,034
There are so many things to see.

1321
00:54:49,954 --> 00:54:52,724
(Walking)

1322
00:54:53,924 --> 00:54:54,993
Gosh, it's so cute!

1323
00:54:54,994 --> 00:54:56,224
(Gosh, it's so cute!)

1324
00:54:56,764 --> 00:54:57,964
So this is it.

1325
00:55:00,734 --> 00:55:01,734
This is it.

1326
00:55:01,735 --> 00:55:02,833
(She even takes a picture.)

1327
00:55:02,834 --> 00:55:03,904
Where is this?

1328
00:55:04,204 --> 00:55:06,673
(The place she came to with a heart full of excitement)

1329
00:55:06,674 --> 00:55:07,733
(Cheonho Stationery and Toy Street)

1330
00:55:07,734 --> 00:55:10,274
- The Stationery Street? - There's a place like this?

1331
00:55:11,444 --> 00:55:14,674
This is Cheonho-dong's Stationery Street.

1332
00:55:14,974 --> 00:55:16,143
(Cheonho Stationery and Toy Street)

1333
00:55:16,144 --> 00:55:17,384
So there's a place like that.

1334
00:55:17,484 --> 00:55:18,913
The Stationery Street is really hot these days.

1335
00:55:18,914 --> 00:55:19,954
- Really? - Yes.

1336
00:55:21,184 --> 00:55:22,553
(The place is filled with stationery and toys.)

1337
00:55:22,554 --> 00:55:24,930
It's been a while since I've seen a stationery store like that.

1338
00:55:24,954 --> 00:55:26,854
(Including various kinds of stationery...)

1339
00:55:28,694 --> 00:55:30,193
The Stationery and Toy Street...

1340
00:55:30,194 --> 00:55:31,323
- in Dongmyo is famous. - Right.

1341
00:55:31,324 --> 00:55:35,134
Some of the owners who were there moved over to this area.

1342
00:55:35,364 --> 00:55:37,364
That was how a new one was formed in Cheonho-dong.

1343
00:55:38,464 --> 00:55:43,344
I'm about to make a big challenge this year.

1344
00:55:43,474 --> 00:55:45,073
I have to study really hard.

1345
00:55:45,074 --> 00:55:48,744
As I'm someone who finds working tools to be important,

1346
00:55:48,984 --> 00:55:52,913
I came to this place to prepare myself...

1347
00:55:52,914 --> 00:55:54,154
with the right supplies.

1348
00:55:54,354 --> 00:55:55,654
Supplies are important.

1349
00:55:59,454 --> 00:56:01,694
- Hello. - Hello.

1350
00:56:02,424 --> 00:56:04,324
Where is the stationery?

1351
00:56:04,894 --> 00:56:06,893
They're over there.

1352
00:56:06,894 --> 00:56:08,064
I see.

1353
00:56:09,534 --> 00:56:12,034
I can imagine how that place smells.

1354
00:56:12,204 --> 00:56:13,433
That particular smell of that store.

1355
00:56:13,434 --> 00:56:14,503
Right.

1356
00:56:14,504 --> 00:56:16,174
- Stationery stores smell nice. - Right.

1357
00:56:17,704 --> 00:56:20,844
(After diligently checking the writing supplies, )

1358
00:56:21,374 --> 00:56:24,684
(she puts in the pens she likes.)

1359
00:56:26,314 --> 00:56:29,524
(She walks inside.)

1360
00:56:30,884 --> 00:56:31,954
What?

1361
00:56:32,824 --> 00:56:34,153
(Prepared mustard)

1362
00:56:34,154 --> 00:56:35,724
- "Prepared mustard?" - "Mustard?"

1363
00:56:35,964 --> 00:56:37,224
Is it an eraser?

1364
00:56:37,594 --> 00:56:39,093
- It's a highlighter. - A highlighter?

1365
00:56:39,094 --> 00:56:40,964
- A highlighter of that color? - Yes.

1366
00:56:41,034 --> 00:56:43,594
- There are many fascinating items. - There are so many of them.

1367
00:56:44,534 --> 00:56:46,873
(She loves it.)

1368
00:56:46,874 --> 00:56:47,904
I like this.

1369
00:56:48,404 --> 00:56:51,873
(Will this one be better?)

1370
00:56:51,874 --> 00:56:53,744
"Cramming from now on."

1371
00:56:54,274 --> 00:56:56,713
It's targeted toward those who don't study.

1372
00:56:56,714 --> 00:56:58,584
- Right. - Right.

1373
00:56:58,914 --> 00:57:00,253
- The studious ones... - Right?

1374
00:57:00,254 --> 00:57:01,313
Are studying instead of going to places like that.

1375
00:57:01,314 --> 00:57:03,923
- Right. - They also use classic pens.

1376
00:57:03,924 --> 00:57:05,183
- Right. - Right.

1377
00:57:05,184 --> 00:57:06,384
They have just what they need.

1378
00:57:07,594 --> 00:57:08,693
I should get this one.

1379
00:57:08,694 --> 00:57:10,570
(She puts in the highlighter that doesn't look classic at all.)

1380
00:57:10,594 --> 00:57:12,063
There were highlighters here as well.

1381
00:57:12,064 --> 00:57:14,164
(She picks up another handful of highlighters.)

1382
00:57:14,994 --> 00:57:16,433
(I must get notebooks as well.)

1383
00:57:16,434 --> 00:57:17,463
That's the most exciting moment.

1384
00:57:17,464 --> 00:57:19,573
Buying notebooks before the new semester.

1385
00:57:19,574 --> 00:57:21,103
"This one is for Korean."

1386
00:57:21,104 --> 00:57:23,573
- Right. - "This one is for English."

1387
00:57:23,574 --> 00:57:24,943
Your name is written on the side.

1388
00:57:24,944 --> 00:57:27,584
- Right. After spreading it out. - Your name is written like that.

1389
00:57:27,614 --> 00:57:29,083
That affection lasts a month.

1390
00:57:29,084 --> 00:57:30,413
- Right. - Right.

1391
00:57:30,414 --> 00:57:31,883
- You get sick of it later. - Right.

1392
00:57:31,884 --> 00:57:33,804
You forget where the notebook has gone later on.

1393
00:57:36,824 --> 00:57:38,684
(Taking a look)

1394
00:57:39,494 --> 00:57:40,594
There are more squishies.

1395
00:57:41,794 --> 00:57:42,794
(Squishies?)

1396
00:57:42,794 --> 00:57:43,794
Squishies!

1397
00:57:43,924 --> 00:57:45,364
I love squishies.

1398
00:57:46,264 --> 00:57:49,363
The slime was popular for a while.

1399
00:57:49,364 --> 00:57:52,264
The squishy has the same texture of the slime,

1400
00:57:52,534 --> 00:57:54,274
but there's an extra layer on the outside.

1401
00:57:54,374 --> 00:57:57,044
It doesn't stick to your hand.

1402
00:57:58,374 --> 00:58:00,343
(The squishy can be carried around and played with.)

1403
00:58:00,344 --> 00:58:01,784
Doesn't it feel nice just to see it?

1404
00:58:02,344 --> 00:58:03,484
It's a stress-reliever.

1405
00:58:03,714 --> 00:58:06,713
- There are pet squishies. - Pet squishies?

1406
00:58:06,714 --> 00:58:09,184
There are a lot of people who carry those around.

1407
00:58:09,284 --> 00:58:12,384
I'm someone who is trend-sensitive.

1408
00:58:13,324 --> 00:58:15,824
That's why I've started collecting squishies recently.

1409
00:58:16,424 --> 00:58:18,570
- So people collect those. - So that's in trend right now.

1410
00:58:18,594 --> 00:58:20,410
They're really popular. Why don't you know them?

1411
00:58:20,434 --> 00:58:22,534
- I know them. - You're no longer the TSM.

1412
00:58:22,764 --> 00:58:24,264
You didn't even listen to my answer.

1413
00:58:24,834 --> 00:58:26,134
I know what squishies are.

1414
00:58:27,034 --> 00:58:28,434
I was worried that...

1415
00:58:28,904 --> 00:58:30,584
- they would get dirty after use. - I see.

1416
00:58:31,474 --> 00:58:33,014
You can squish your face.

1417
00:58:33,474 --> 00:58:34,774
The Mooshy.

1418
00:58:36,684 --> 00:58:39,284
(Hesitating)

1419
00:58:40,014 --> 00:58:42,554
(I want to get a squishy.)

1420
00:58:42,924 --> 00:58:44,723
I'm here to buy stationery.

1421
00:58:44,724 --> 00:58:45,854
(Let's get to my senses.)

1422
00:58:46,294 --> 00:58:49,164
(She focuses on buying stationery after feeling tempted.)

1423
00:58:49,924 --> 00:58:51,124
There are more squishies here!

1424
00:58:53,234 --> 00:58:54,234
It's a potato.

1425
00:58:56,134 --> 00:58:57,203
(Squishing)

1426
00:58:57,204 --> 00:58:58,884
- It's the potato bun! - That one is cute.

1427
00:58:59,434 --> 00:59:02,234
(Eyes rolling)

1428
00:59:03,204 --> 00:59:06,774
(It goes into the basket.)

1429
00:59:07,014 --> 00:59:09,484
Gosh. I like all of them.

1430
00:59:10,984 --> 00:59:14,114
It's those times when I feel like a successful adult.

1431
00:59:14,554 --> 00:59:15,783
- I keep getting reminded... - Right.

1432
00:59:15,784 --> 00:59:17,024
- Right. - of my childhood.

1433
00:59:18,684 --> 00:59:20,554
(Chuckling)

1434
00:59:21,024 --> 00:59:22,093
(She spots a squishy that is shaped like a face.)

1435
00:59:22,094 --> 00:59:23,334
- What is that? - What is that?

1436
00:59:24,064 --> 00:59:25,864
It looks like someone.

1437
00:59:27,294 --> 00:59:28,294
It looks...

1438
00:59:28,295 --> 00:59:29,803
(Looking closely)

1439
00:59:29,804 --> 00:59:31,433
a bit like Jun Hyun Moo.

1440
00:59:31,434 --> 00:59:33,734
(It looks like Jun Hyun Moo.)

1441
00:59:34,304 --> 00:59:35,603
(Even the Mooshy gets put into the basket.)

1442
00:59:35,604 --> 00:59:38,303
- I ended up buying so many things. - That's a lot of things.

1443
00:59:38,304 --> 00:59:42,044
(She finally heads to the counter!)

1444
00:59:46,014 --> 00:59:47,583
(The basket is filled with toys instead of stationery.)

1445
00:59:47,584 --> 00:59:48,953
- There are so many of them. - There are so many of them.

1446
00:59:48,954 --> 00:59:50,314
I ended up buying so many of them.

1447
00:59:52,424 --> 00:59:55,294
I've been trying to live like a minimalist.

1448
00:59:56,094 --> 00:59:57,293
- What are you saying? - I'm serious!

1449
00:59:57,294 --> 00:59:59,334
I shared the things I had...

1450
00:59:59,464 --> 01:00:01,034
and refrained from buying things.

1451
01:00:01,234 --> 01:00:03,354
But I couldn't stop myself from buying the squishies.

1452
01:00:03,404 --> 01:00:05,304
They might end up being sold at the bazaar.

1453
01:00:07,034 --> 01:00:08,803
They're going to appear without being opened.

1454
01:00:08,804 --> 01:00:10,943
That is how we get a lot of things at the bazaar.

1455
01:00:10,944 --> 01:00:12,304
- I got it now. - Right.

1456
01:00:13,114 --> 01:00:15,113
(The loaded basket gets checked out.)

1457
01:00:15,114 --> 01:00:16,714
You've bought a lot of different things.

1458
01:00:16,884 --> 01:00:18,543
(Feeling proud)

1459
01:00:18,544 --> 01:00:19,554
One of these.

1460
01:00:20,554 --> 01:00:23,424
(The squishies get checked out endlessly.)

1461
01:00:23,524 --> 01:00:25,484
- You must be a big spender. - Right.

1462
01:00:26,124 --> 01:00:27,224
The maximalist.

1463
01:00:29,194 --> 01:00:30,963
- Gosh. - Here's the receipt.

1464
01:00:30,964 --> 01:00:32,194
I bought so many things.

1465
01:00:32,734 --> 01:00:33,994
She's living her dream.

1466
01:00:34,994 --> 01:00:36,133
- Thank you. - People like her and me...

1467
01:00:36,134 --> 01:00:37,403
are making the economy flow.

1468
01:00:37,404 --> 01:00:39,524
(People like her and me are making the economy flow.)

1469
01:00:40,474 --> 01:00:43,244
(She successfully makes the economy flow.)

1470
01:00:44,574 --> 01:00:47,374
(Struggling)

1471
01:00:48,914 --> 01:00:51,384
(She feels great.)

1472
01:00:52,914 --> 01:00:56,024
(She arrives somewhere while humming.)

1473
01:00:57,157 --> 01:00:58,227
It's not her home.

1474
01:00:59,127 --> 01:01:01,297
- Hello. - Hi.

1475
01:01:02,397 --> 01:01:03,737
(Tapping)

1476
01:01:04,097 --> 01:01:05,707
Welcome, Ms. Park Soo Young.

1477
01:01:06,837 --> 01:01:09,677
- Can I keep this somewhere? - Sure.

1478
01:01:09,877 --> 01:01:11,237
- Give it to me. - Thank you.

1479
01:01:12,177 --> 01:01:14,507
(Striding inside after keeping her stuff)

1480
01:01:15,247 --> 01:01:17,577
- Please put on your name tag. - Okay.

1481
01:01:18,917 --> 01:01:21,447
(Behind Joy who settles herself naturally...)

1482
01:01:24,917 --> 01:01:27,426
This is a pet grooming school.

1483
01:01:27,427 --> 01:01:30,196
It's where you learn and train...

1484
01:01:30,197 --> 01:01:32,666
to get a pet groomer certification.

1485
01:01:32,667 --> 01:01:34,526
(Where she comes to study these days)

1486
01:01:34,527 --> 01:01:37,766
I started coming here as soon as...

1487
01:01:37,767 --> 01:01:39,006
my drama shoot was done.

1488
01:01:39,007 --> 01:01:41,706
I went to register myself the next day...

1489
01:01:41,707 --> 01:01:43,147
right after the drama wrap-up party.

1490
01:01:43,307 --> 01:01:46,246
It's been around two months.

1491
01:01:46,247 --> 01:01:47,406
(It's been 2 months since she started going to the school.)

1492
01:01:47,407 --> 01:01:50,276
I always think about what ifs.

1493
01:01:50,277 --> 01:01:52,687
"If I can't continue..."

1494
01:01:52,817 --> 01:01:55,787
"with this career,"

1495
01:01:55,917 --> 01:01:58,726
"how should I live on?" I had such a thought.

1496
01:01:58,727 --> 01:02:02,727
I thought it'd be nice to have some sort of skills.

1497
01:02:03,397 --> 01:02:05,897
Since I love dogs,

1498
01:02:06,027 --> 01:02:07,967
I decided to learn pet grooming.

1499
01:02:08,167 --> 01:02:10,737
That's how I started this.

1500
01:02:11,397 --> 01:02:13,737
Isn't it helpful in real life too?

1501
01:02:13,937 --> 01:02:16,507
Yes, I can groom my dog too.

1502
01:02:16,837 --> 01:02:18,306
It's good for dog shelter volunteering too.

1503
01:02:18,307 --> 01:02:19,576
The chance of getting adopted...

1504
01:02:19,577 --> 01:02:21,046
- That's right. - goes up high.

1505
01:02:21,047 --> 01:02:22,746
- That's a good thing. - If you groom them a bit...

1506
01:02:22,747 --> 01:02:25,587
- I wanted to do the volunteering. - Totally.

1507
01:02:25,817 --> 01:02:28,757
There are written and practical exams.

1508
01:02:28,887 --> 01:02:31,756
The number of times you can take them...

1509
01:02:31,757 --> 01:02:33,757
is four only.

1510
01:02:34,327 --> 01:02:36,997
There's a written exam in July.

1511
01:02:38,097 --> 01:02:42,337
First, to prepare for the practical exam,

1512
01:02:42,767 --> 01:02:46,207
I've been going there 10 times within 2 months to learn.

1513
01:02:46,937 --> 01:02:50,507
(A shapeless white fluff ball)

1514
01:02:50,607 --> 01:02:51,706
She worked hard.

1515
01:02:51,707 --> 01:02:53,707
(She started learning to cut it in a heart shape.)

1516
01:02:54,747 --> 01:02:57,446
(After a long practice, )

1517
01:02:57,447 --> 01:02:58,447
(Joy managed to turn it into a dog shape.)

1518
01:02:58,448 --> 01:03:00,917
It's learning to make a poodle shape.

1519
01:03:01,847 --> 01:03:04,187
Making a poodle is a practical exam.

1520
01:03:04,387 --> 01:03:06,826
There are 1st-stage grooming and 2nd-stage grooming.

1521
01:03:06,827 --> 01:03:08,556
- As for 1st-stage... - You need a 1st-stage grooming?

1522
01:03:08,557 --> 01:03:10,857
You need to brush and straighten...

1523
01:03:11,357 --> 01:03:14,097
the white fluff ball at first.

1524
01:03:14,297 --> 01:03:16,366
Then you do the first-stage grooming.

1525
01:03:16,367 --> 01:03:19,137
Then you do the second stage, which is shaping the fur.

1526
01:03:19,267 --> 01:03:21,166
You need to finish the whole process...

1527
01:03:21,167 --> 01:03:23,037
within two and a half hours during the exam.

1528
01:03:23,237 --> 01:03:25,237
But it took me 6 hours for the 1st-stage grooming.

1529
01:03:26,147 --> 01:03:28,847
I did 2nd-stage grooming for 5 hours the day before.

1530
01:03:28,977 --> 01:03:30,647
That day, I went to wrap up.

1531
01:03:31,517 --> 01:03:33,346
Since you're done with the 1st and 2nd-stage grooming,

1532
01:03:33,347 --> 01:03:36,887
- Yes. Okay. - you'll do the tail and ears today.

1533
01:03:37,087 --> 01:03:38,117
Good luck.

1534
01:03:38,287 --> 01:03:39,287
(Good luck to me.)

1535
01:03:39,288 --> 01:03:41,427
- I think you'll complete it today. - Okay.

1536
01:03:42,957 --> 01:03:45,867
(Quickly taking out the tools)

1537
01:03:46,297 --> 01:03:49,466
(Ready to practice grooming)

1538
01:03:49,467 --> 01:03:50,636
It looks like...

1539
01:03:50,637 --> 01:03:51,796
- I've trimmed it a lot. - Yes.

1540
01:03:51,797 --> 01:03:53,966
- But it's far from done. - Isn't that good already?

1541
01:03:53,967 --> 01:03:55,006
No, I'm far from done.

1542
01:03:55,007 --> 01:03:56,576
- It looks like a real dog. - Yes.

1543
01:03:56,577 --> 01:03:58,677
It looks like a living dog.

1544
01:03:59,007 --> 01:04:00,007
(Let's see.)

1545
01:04:00,008 --> 01:04:01,047
From here...

1546
01:04:02,447 --> 01:04:06,347
(She takes a quick look and cuts it.)

1547
01:04:07,687 --> 01:04:09,516
(She's quite skilled with scissors...)

1548
01:04:09,517 --> 01:04:11,317
(as she's been practicing for two months.)

1549
01:04:12,927 --> 01:04:14,057
It's fun.

1550
01:04:14,257 --> 01:04:16,757
When I'm practicing grooming,

1551
01:04:16,927 --> 01:04:19,326
it feels like an hour has passed,

1552
01:04:19,327 --> 01:04:20,627
but four hours have been gone.

1553
01:04:23,567 --> 01:04:27,667
(She continues grooming with scissors with one hand.)

1554
01:04:27,837 --> 01:04:29,117
You have to hold the nose of it.

1555
01:04:29,277 --> 01:04:30,306
Just now,

1556
01:04:30,307 --> 01:04:31,736
- you held scissors with one hand... - Yes.

1557
01:04:31,737 --> 01:04:33,507
- and a brush with another, right? - Yes.

1558
01:04:33,747 --> 01:04:36,447
(Joy used the scissors with one hand earlier.)

1559
01:04:36,917 --> 01:04:38,947
- You can't do that, can you? - Right.

1560
01:04:39,317 --> 01:04:40,816
- You can't do that, can you? - Right.

1561
01:04:40,817 --> 01:04:41,947
- She's so scary. - Right.

1562
01:04:42,687 --> 01:04:44,656
You must hold the nose with the other hand.

1563
01:04:44,657 --> 01:04:46,326
- You must do that. It's dangerous. - That's right.

1564
01:04:46,327 --> 01:04:47,767
That's how a teacher should be like.

1565
01:04:47,857 --> 01:04:48,857
That way, you learn faster.

1566
01:04:48,858 --> 01:04:50,126
- Otherwise, a dog could get hurt. - Here's why you hold the snout.

1567
01:04:50,127 --> 01:04:52,197
- A dog could fall off the table. - Right.

1568
01:04:52,367 --> 01:04:54,797
If it falls, then you're disqualified.

1569
01:04:54,897 --> 01:04:56,836
- So always hold the snout, - Yes.

1570
01:04:56,837 --> 01:04:58,706
- Yes. - and fix it.

1571
01:04:58,707 --> 01:05:00,406
You must always hold the snout.

1572
01:05:00,407 --> 01:05:01,766
What if it bites?

1573
01:05:01,767 --> 01:05:02,806
What if it goes like this?

1574
01:05:02,807 --> 01:05:04,336
- You use a real dog for the exam? - No.

1575
01:05:04,337 --> 01:05:06,523
- We use that for the exam too. - Right. That doesn't make sense.

1576
01:05:06,547 --> 01:05:08,947
(Joy got feedback from the instructor.)

1577
01:05:09,177 --> 01:05:11,617
(Let me try it again.)

1578
01:05:11,777 --> 01:05:12,816
There you go.

1579
01:05:12,817 --> 01:05:15,217
(Holding the snout first as the instructor told her)

1580
01:05:15,557 --> 01:05:17,257
- It's hard. - This isn't easy.

1581
01:05:17,517 --> 01:05:19,026
- It must be hard. - Yes.

1582
01:05:19,027 --> 01:05:20,427
(She carefully continues grooming.)

1583
01:05:20,757 --> 01:05:22,757
(Glancing)

1584
01:05:24,857 --> 01:05:26,366
(The other classmates seem skilled.)

1585
01:05:26,367 --> 01:05:28,567
There are many male students too.

1586
01:05:28,867 --> 01:05:30,987
There are people of all ages and gender in the class.

1587
01:05:32,067 --> 01:05:33,736
- She's really good. - Yes.

1588
01:05:33,737 --> 01:05:34,807
- Goodness. - Gosh.

1589
01:05:37,007 --> 01:05:41,077
(She gets motivated and starts again with a new mindset.)

1590
01:05:42,677 --> 01:05:47,547
(Her back gets hunched more as time goes by.)

1591
01:05:48,687 --> 01:05:50,256
(In the end, she stands in a weird posture.)

1592
01:05:50,257 --> 01:05:52,427
The instructor told me I should stand like that.

1593
01:05:52,827 --> 01:05:54,757
That's cool. You look like an artist.

1594
01:05:55,727 --> 01:05:57,727
(Serious)

1595
01:06:00,227 --> 01:06:01,296
Gosh, her back must hurt.

1596
01:06:01,297 --> 01:06:02,437
Her back must hurt.

1597
01:06:02,997 --> 01:06:04,996
- Your back must hurt. - It really does.

1598
01:06:04,997 --> 01:06:07,037
My back and neck hurt so much.

1599
01:06:08,137 --> 01:06:10,607
(Now, she's almost crawling.)

1600
01:06:11,107 --> 01:06:12,576
The instructor is so scary.

1601
01:06:12,577 --> 01:06:13,646
(The instructor is watching her from afar.)

1602
01:06:13,647 --> 01:06:14,876
- She's so scary. - She must not like...

1603
01:06:14,877 --> 01:06:16,116
what you're doing.

1604
01:06:16,117 --> 01:06:18,987
(Staring quietly)

1605
01:06:19,587 --> 01:06:21,046
(Approaching)

1606
01:06:21,047 --> 01:06:22,287
That's the most nerve-racking.

1607
01:06:22,787 --> 01:06:25,117
- I've been watching you from afar. - Yes.

1608
01:06:25,587 --> 01:06:28,086
The name of the scissors is blades without movements.

1609
01:06:28,087 --> 01:06:29,757
- Yes. - So it has to be fixed.

1610
01:06:29,927 --> 01:06:31,926
But you are putting it close to the dog,

1611
01:06:31,927 --> 01:06:33,897
and moving like this without it touching the dog.

1612
01:06:34,067 --> 01:06:36,496
After that, the fur will keep sticking out...

1613
01:06:36,497 --> 01:06:38,766
- when you brush it. - Yes, it keeps doing that.

1614
01:06:38,767 --> 01:06:42,007
Right? That's because you pushed it down instead of cutting.

1615
01:06:42,437 --> 01:06:44,106
It's completely different...

1616
01:06:44,107 --> 01:06:45,777
- from normal trimming. - I can see that.

1617
01:06:46,147 --> 01:06:49,317
That kind of trimming is called fixed blades.

1618
01:06:49,847 --> 01:06:52,186
You must fix the top blade,

1619
01:06:52,187 --> 01:06:54,417
- and move with the down blade only. - You're right.

1620
01:06:55,017 --> 01:06:56,556
That's really hard.

1621
01:06:56,557 --> 01:07:00,587
So on the 1st day, I only practiced that trimming for 2 hours.

1622
01:07:00,987 --> 01:07:02,496
I practiced that only.

1623
01:07:02,497 --> 01:07:03,827
- Oh, like that? - Oh, that?

1624
01:07:04,297 --> 01:07:06,343
- You must fix the top blade. - It must make your hand numb.

1625
01:07:06,367 --> 01:07:08,627
It makes your hand numb. You get calluses here.

1626
01:07:09,237 --> 01:07:11,697
It's different from my way of grooming.

1627
01:07:11,997 --> 01:07:13,037
Sorry?

1628
01:07:13,767 --> 01:07:17,037
(Doubleblade84 cuts his hair with no order.)

1629
01:07:17,307 --> 01:07:18,953
I've been cutting my own hair for ten years.

1630
01:07:18,977 --> 01:07:20,307
(Feeling proud)

1631
01:07:21,107 --> 01:07:23,347
(Unlike Doubleblade84)

1632
01:07:23,817 --> 01:07:27,917
(she's grooming the dog with top blade fixed.)

1633
01:07:30,017 --> 01:07:31,857
Gosh, ma'am!

1634
01:07:32,227 --> 01:07:33,426
(Observing her from behind)

1635
01:07:33,427 --> 01:07:35,086
- She's a good instructor. - You should listen to her.

1636
01:07:35,087 --> 01:07:36,807
- You're right. - That's how one should be.

1637
01:07:39,927 --> 01:07:41,066
Gosh, it's tiring.

1638
01:07:41,067 --> 01:07:43,096
Ma'am, what should I do now?

1639
01:07:43,097 --> 01:07:44,537
I was startled.

1640
01:07:47,707 --> 01:07:48,906
Should I trim more?

1641
01:07:48,907 --> 01:07:51,037
(Coming close to Joy)

1642
01:07:52,247 --> 01:07:53,307
What is it?

1643
01:07:53,547 --> 01:07:54,646
She laughs too.

1644
01:07:54,647 --> 01:07:55,776
What you need to pay attention to...

1645
01:07:55,777 --> 01:07:56,916
- is scissors. - Yes.

1646
01:07:56,917 --> 01:07:58,216
You'll be trimming a real dog...

1647
01:07:58,217 --> 01:07:59,516
- in the future. - Yes.

1648
01:07:59,517 --> 01:08:02,317
It shouldn't be dangerous when you trim a real dog.

1649
01:08:02,487 --> 01:08:05,156
It'll be better if you fix the top blade a bit more.

1650
01:08:05,157 --> 01:08:06,626
- That must be really important. - Fixing the top blade.

1651
01:08:06,627 --> 01:08:08,226
If you don't want to hurt the dog...

1652
01:08:08,227 --> 01:08:09,296
Also, shake off the tail fur...

1653
01:08:09,297 --> 01:08:10,326
- as well. - Okay.

1654
01:08:10,327 --> 01:08:11,396
I'll teach you how to trim...

1655
01:08:11,397 --> 01:08:12,797
- the tail properly later. - Okay.

1656
01:08:13,197 --> 01:08:15,096
- It says "Fix the top blade..." - Yes.

1657
01:08:15,097 --> 01:08:16,396
In red on the wall.

1658
01:08:16,397 --> 01:08:18,196
- Yes, it's the most important. - It must be really important.

1659
01:08:18,197 --> 01:08:19,706
- It must be important. - Like a class motto.

1660
01:08:19,707 --> 01:08:21,306
- Right. - Look. "Fix the top blade."

1661
01:08:21,307 --> 01:08:23,877
- "Fix the top blade." - There's a competition on that too.

1662
01:08:24,307 --> 01:08:25,607
- Really? - Yes.

1663
01:08:27,307 --> 01:08:28,977
(Flopping)

1664
01:08:30,177 --> 01:08:32,017
(Gosh, I'm tired.)

1665
01:08:32,947 --> 01:08:35,187
(Taking a glance at other classmates)

1666
01:08:35,957 --> 01:08:37,656
I thought, "This is so tough,"

1667
01:08:37,657 --> 01:08:40,757
"but they're managing it?"

1668
01:08:41,457 --> 01:08:42,756
(They're all so good.)

1669
01:08:42,757 --> 01:08:43,796
Are you jealous?

1670
01:08:43,797 --> 01:08:45,427
(Glancing)

1671
01:08:46,397 --> 01:08:48,127
It took me a month to finish a dog.

1672
01:08:48,327 --> 01:08:49,396
- Really? - Yes.

1673
01:08:49,397 --> 01:08:51,737
I didn't know it was so hard before I began learning it.

1674
01:08:52,067 --> 01:08:54,936
You're pretty good, considering how it's your first time.

1675
01:08:54,937 --> 01:08:56,537
- She's so kind. - Right.

1676
01:08:57,077 --> 01:08:58,947
Really? I...

1677
01:08:59,477 --> 01:09:00,957
It gets better when you finish three.

1678
01:09:01,047 --> 01:09:04,517
It gets better if I finish three dogs?

1679
01:09:04,617 --> 01:09:07,016
You get better as your skills improve.

1680
01:09:07,017 --> 01:09:09,056
- Really? - If you finish this,

1681
01:09:09,057 --> 01:09:10,456
- you'll get the hang of it soon. - Yes.

1682
01:09:10,457 --> 01:09:11,616
Your skills improve.

1683
01:09:11,617 --> 01:09:14,187
I only got scolded today.

1684
01:09:14,627 --> 01:09:16,127
I kept getting scolded too.

1685
01:09:17,127 --> 01:09:18,557
When did I scold you?

1686
01:09:18,757 --> 01:09:20,196
She was listening.

1687
01:09:20,197 --> 01:09:23,367
(I didn't scold you.)

1688
01:09:23,537 --> 01:09:25,166
I was scolded quite a lot today too.

1689
01:09:25,167 --> 01:09:27,337
(Amicable)

1690
01:09:29,677 --> 01:09:31,537
It became really hairy when I brushed it.

1691
01:09:31,777 --> 01:09:33,477
- You're right. - That's the tail.

1692
01:09:34,807 --> 01:09:37,777
(Getting into it in earnest after boosting her confidence)

1693
01:09:39,617 --> 01:09:41,787
(Focused)

1694
01:09:45,417 --> 01:09:50,027
(Steady focus)

1695
01:09:53,127 --> 01:09:54,967
I practiced for two and a half hours that day.

1696
01:09:56,137 --> 01:09:57,966
(Model dog slowly taking shape)

1697
01:09:57,967 --> 01:09:59,006
The tail is cute!

1698
01:09:59,007 --> 01:10:00,437
It's like a balloon dog.

1699
01:10:00,837 --> 01:10:01,906
A dog made of balloon.

1700
01:10:01,907 --> 01:10:03,207
- Right. - I know.

1701
01:10:03,277 --> 01:10:04,437
A dog balloon.

1702
01:10:06,847 --> 01:10:09,007
You did a good job meeting the right size of the tail.

1703
01:10:09,347 --> 01:10:11,477
- As for the edges, - Yes.

1704
01:10:11,677 --> 01:10:14,417
You can trim it a bit.

1705
01:10:14,917 --> 01:10:17,616
You'll be done with it if you complete the tail.

1706
01:10:17,617 --> 01:10:19,557
- It'll be done finally? - You'll be done.

1707
01:10:20,157 --> 01:10:21,257
Great job.

1708
01:10:21,887 --> 01:10:23,457
It's Minky.

1709
01:10:23,727 --> 01:10:25,256
- It's pretty. - It's cute.

1710
01:10:25,257 --> 01:10:26,426
Minky is cute, right?

1711
01:10:26,427 --> 01:10:29,236
(She finally completed her first model dog.)

1712
01:10:29,237 --> 01:10:31,567
- Great job, really. - It's so tiring.

1713
01:10:32,607 --> 01:10:34,766
(A triumphant masterpiece)

1714
01:10:34,767 --> 01:10:35,776
Minky!

1715
01:10:35,777 --> 01:10:37,636
I hung my name tag.

1716
01:10:37,637 --> 01:10:39,106
- I'm so proud of it. - I got goosebumps.

1717
01:10:39,107 --> 01:10:40,107
Right.

1718
01:10:42,917 --> 01:10:44,047
I'm not happy with it.

1719
01:10:44,377 --> 01:10:45,377
Why not?

1720
01:10:45,378 --> 01:10:47,087
Gosh, seriously...

1721
01:10:47,217 --> 01:10:51,157
I clearly cut it nicely and well with scissors.

1722
01:10:51,317 --> 01:10:53,227
But when you brush it,

1723
01:10:53,687 --> 01:10:57,057
the hidden fur keeps coming out.

1724
01:10:57,827 --> 01:10:59,297
There was a big difference.

1725
01:10:59,597 --> 01:11:01,896
I tried my best to imitate it,

1726
01:11:01,897 --> 01:11:04,637
and I worked hard to follow.

1727
01:11:04,667 --> 01:11:07,306
It does look more condensed.

1728
01:11:07,307 --> 01:11:08,867
- That's neater. - You're right.

1729
01:11:09,207 --> 01:11:10,737
Joy's is more like a sheep.

1730
01:11:11,877 --> 01:11:13,106
- Right? - Dogs like that are cuter...

1731
01:11:13,107 --> 01:11:14,306
in real life.

1732
01:11:14,307 --> 01:11:15,946
- That's true. - They need to be lacking.

1733
01:11:15,947 --> 01:11:18,017
- That's right. It's too smooth. - Right.

1734
01:11:18,547 --> 01:11:21,717
It's really hard.

1735
01:11:22,017 --> 01:11:24,687
We often take our dogs to a groomer.

1736
01:11:24,917 --> 01:11:27,887
They should charge 1,000 dollars per dog.

1737
01:11:29,627 --> 01:11:31,633
- What are you talking about? - The value of labor.

1738
01:11:31,657 --> 01:11:33,526
I worked myself to the bone.

1739
01:11:33,527 --> 01:11:37,397
I poured my all, passion, and spirits into it.

1740
01:11:39,507 --> 01:11:42,437
(Cleaning up after completing her dog)

1741
01:11:43,277 --> 01:11:45,977
(Let's go, Minky.)

1742
01:11:47,107 --> 01:11:48,107
(Bumping)

1743
01:11:48,108 --> 01:11:50,716
- Oh, dear. - No. Minky's leg broke.

1744
01:11:50,717 --> 01:11:51,816
She's treating it horribly.

1745
01:11:51,817 --> 01:11:53,246
At that rate, its kneecap popped out.

1746
01:11:53,247 --> 01:11:54,447
No way.

1747
01:11:57,317 --> 01:11:58,587
- Thank you. - Sure.

1748
01:12:00,387 --> 01:12:02,827
- Great job. - Right. Thank you.

1749
01:12:04,727 --> 01:12:06,166
(Joy came outside.)

1750
01:12:06,167 --> 01:12:07,526
She must be exhausted.

1751
01:12:07,527 --> 01:12:08,597
The sun has set.

1752
01:12:08,967 --> 01:12:11,797
(Tired)

1753
01:12:14,607 --> 01:12:17,677
(The long-awaited taxi is here.)

1754
01:12:19,977 --> 01:12:22,547
- Hello. - Welcome.

1755
01:12:25,817 --> 01:12:27,786
(Squishing)

1756
01:12:27,787 --> 01:12:28,886
For peace of mind.

1757
01:12:28,887 --> 01:12:29,986
- Seriously. - There's a reason...

1758
01:12:29,987 --> 01:12:31,463
- why she bought that a lot. - Seriously.

1759
01:12:31,487 --> 01:12:32,627
I get her now.

1760
01:12:35,057 --> 01:12:37,597
(She passed out soon.)

1761
01:12:38,097 --> 01:12:40,297
- I was exhausted. - Seriously.

1762
01:12:41,297 --> 01:12:42,966
You're tired because you bought that much.

1763
01:12:42,967 --> 01:12:44,266
That's not true.

1764
01:12:44,267 --> 01:12:45,566
- Grooming was the hard part. - You went around a lot.

1765
01:12:45,567 --> 01:12:47,367
They'd think you're selling the squish balls.

1766
01:12:48,937 --> 01:12:50,306
(Joy became completely worn out...)

1767
01:12:50,307 --> 01:12:52,227
(after a two-and-a-half-hour grueling schedule.)

1768
01:12:53,777 --> 01:12:56,916
(She came home after an exhausting day.)

1769
01:12:56,917 --> 01:12:58,777
Look who's here?

1770
01:12:59,147 --> 01:13:00,246
(Barking)

1771
01:13:00,247 --> 01:13:02,347
Look who's here?

1772
01:13:03,857 --> 01:13:05,557
Come here.

1773
01:13:06,907 --> 01:13:08,637
Come here.

1774
01:13:09,407 --> 01:13:10,407
- My baby. - Oh, my.

1775
01:13:12,547 --> 01:13:14,777
My pretty baby.

1776
01:13:15,207 --> 01:13:16,917
It's my baby, Haetnim.

1777
01:13:17,877 --> 01:13:20,017
It's a female dog, and she's eight this year.

1778
01:13:20,687 --> 01:13:21,816
(Hi.)

1779
01:13:21,817 --> 01:13:23,416
- She's cute, right? - She's cute.

1780
01:13:23,417 --> 01:13:26,087
She's a dog raised at my parents' house,

1781
01:13:26,627 --> 01:13:27,763
but she comes to my place often.

1782
01:13:27,787 --> 01:13:29,727
She's a Maltese.

1783
01:13:29,957 --> 01:13:32,567
She's got the typical Maltese sass.

1784
01:13:32,767 --> 01:13:34,497
But she's really gentle.

1785
01:13:35,127 --> 01:13:36,766
She's really kind.

1786
01:13:36,767 --> 01:13:38,397
And she's a really pretty dog.

1787
01:13:41,537 --> 01:13:42,576
How cute.

1788
01:13:42,577 --> 01:13:43,707
(Doting on her)

1789
01:13:44,307 --> 01:13:45,377
I'm tired.

1790
01:13:45,847 --> 01:13:47,007
Haetnim, I'm tired.

1791
01:13:47,577 --> 01:13:48,847
Haetnim, I'm tired.

1792
01:13:51,047 --> 01:13:54,686
(Joy passes out after a long training.)

1793
01:13:54,687 --> 01:13:55,717
I'm so tired.

1794
01:13:56,087 --> 01:13:57,556
(Knocked out in front of Haetnim)

1795
01:13:57,557 --> 01:13:58,557
Haetnim.

1796
01:13:59,127 --> 01:14:00,157
Haetnim.

1797
01:14:03,327 --> 01:14:07,727
(I should get up.)

1798
01:14:09,197 --> 01:14:10,566
Haetnim, are you hungry?

1799
01:14:10,567 --> 01:14:11,567
(Yes!)

1800
01:14:11,568 --> 01:14:12,667
Haetnim, are you hungry?

1801
01:14:14,807 --> 01:14:18,407
(She heads straight to the kitchen.)

1802
01:14:21,077 --> 01:14:22,246
Haetnim.

1803
01:14:22,247 --> 01:14:24,617
(I should feed Haetnim.)

1804
01:14:30,217 --> 01:14:33,587
(A special menu for Haetnim)

1805
